  (:id "message-form/schema-go-base-gotable-and-go-leg-green" :type :task :title "Go dogfood base: wide text, message vocabulary and a C-skipped conformance leg" :state :todo :evidence nil :sprint-card "schema-go-base-gotable-and-go-leg-green" :sprint-stream "schema-go" :sprint-base "sprint/schema-go" :note "Attempt 3 at base 2313a5c3: TestFixedFormWideTextCodeUnits, TestMessageWriter and TestSkippedLegIsNotAConformancePrerequisite each failed at base and passed after the scoped changes. The wide-text reader follows SPEC-TABLES.md 3.4 and FIXED-FORM-ALGORITHM.md 4.5; the test forge now fills newly used code units instead of presenting invalid zero text. The compiled message entry uses zero bits for kinds 0 and 32 per SPEC-TABLES.md 3.3. The C conformance prerequisite now honors SCHEMA_SKIP_LEGS=c. A Go-only conformance diagnostic passed every Go surface. The exact requested make conformance command still builds Rust despite its skip because make/rust.mk is unguarded; the full Go package gate also meets an unavailable go1.26.0 pin, and compiler has independent base-red C, JavaScript and list-carrier tests. Those gates remain open; the C emitter's uint0_t bug is outside this Go card.")
  (:id "schema-go-port-completion" :type :work-set :title "Finish the Go port of the schema message form and its checks" :note "Bring the Go generator to the full message form: announcements, batches, versioning, evolution, bounds, writes, integers, floats, unions and optionals, with conformance driver rows for every manifest row. Each step is closed by a test that ran red or bit and then green." :origin "card from the sprint store (2026-10-10)" :release "after v1.4" :children ("message-form/schema-go-msg-fixed-only" "message-form/schema-go-msg-goldens" "message-form/schema-go-msg-strict" "message-form/schema-go-msg-versioning" "message-form/schema-go-t04-versions-evolutionb" "message-form/schema-go-t05-evolution" "message-form/schema-go-t06-bounds" "message-form/schema-go-t07-writes" "message-form/schema-go-t08-writes-conformance" "message-form/schema-go-t09-integers-floats" "message-form/schema-go-t10-floats-composites" "message-form/schema-go-t11-unions-optionals" "schema-go-base-compiler-tests-green" "message-form/schema-go-base-gotable-and-go-leg-green"))
  (:id "schema-go-base-compiler-tests-green" :type :task :title "Schema-go base compiler tests green (guard)" :state :done :evidence ("compiler/tablesgo_test.go TestGoTableWidenFloatFollowsDeclaredKind11" "compiler/tableslists_test.go TestListCarriers" "compiler/tableslists_test.go TestListRefusalNamesTheCarrier" "compiler/tablesjs_test.go TestJsTableModuleScopeNamesAreClaimed") :note "All four base reds are green at the branch head, each shown red at the card's BASE first. (1) TestGoTableWidenFloatFollowsDeclaredKind11: the emitter side was wrong; the declared-kind census in internal/codegen/gotable/wire.go already emits tableWidenFloat and its call only for a unit that declares kind 11 and keeps tableKindWidens in every unit, but the runtime text the emitter carries in internal/codegen/gotable/fixedruntime.go (in this card's PATHS) still named tableWidenFloat in a comment (docs/SPEC-TABLES.md 3.4, 21.2), so a unit that declares no kind 11 emitted the name and tripped the test's substring check; the comment now says float-widen helper, the claim in internal/tablenames/go.go stands. (2,3) TestListCarriers and TestListRefusalNamesTheCarrier: the tests were stale; nine targets carry the unbounded-array codec (docs/SPEC-TABLES.md 2.9), so listTargets is [c cpp cs dart elixir go java js rust] and refuseLists refuses only a non-carrier (zig), and the expectations were corrected to the landed codecs. (4) TestJsTableModuleScopeNamesAreClaimed: the front end's claim was wrong; every module-scope binding of the JavaScript message and batch forms is now claimed in internal/tablenames/js.go (docs/SPEC-TABLES.md 11), so the checker refuses a colliding declaration. The ./compiler reds that remain (TestNewLegLuaFixturePasses, TestTableClosureCountDefaults) are environment facts, missing sibling serialize checkouts, and fail identically at BASE; they are not this card's clause and this card's work did not change them.")
