  ; Saved from sprint epoch 19, 2026-10-12: the 19 open cards of the card variable-table work (streams schema-vt-core and schema-vt-<lang>), grouped under the work-set "card-variable-tables" at the end of this list.
  (:id "cards/tla-card-records-keep-every-field-across-language-hops" :type :task :title "TLA+: card records keep every field across language hops (tla/CardHops.tla)" :state :doing :evidence nil :sprint-card "tla-card-records-keep-every-field-across-language-hops" :sprint-column "working" :sprint-stream "schema-vt-core" :sprint-base "sprint/schema-vt-core" :tier "heavy" :needs ("tla-cardversioning-no-field-is-lost" "the-card-wall-lets-a-tlc-step-read-the-jar-and-java") :pushed-head "08aac1912384490ceadb077283ebb402480e54d3" :pushed-branch "sprint/tla-card-records-keep-every-field-across-language-hops.w1.g2.e19" :note "Saved from the sprint store on 2026-10-12 (epoch 19) before the clear; not landed. Task: model a record crossing builds of different languages and declarations (two legs, two declarations; Write, Read, Upgrade, Edit, Hash) with TypeOK, NoFieldLost, BodyUnchanged, RefusalKeepsOriginal, ImplementationsAgree, HopOrderIrrelevant and TaskHashStable, plus four reversed cfgs each failing its one named invariant, runs recorded in tla/RUNS.tsv. Needs (both landed): tla-cardversioning-no-field-is-lost, the-card-wall-lets-a-tlc-step-read-the-jar-and-java. Order: second of three in schema-vt-core, after the-card-corpus-is-a-language-neutral-conformance-set in the line, and needed by it. WORK EXISTS: attempt 1 pushed head 08aac1912384490ceadb077283ebb402480e54d3 on branch sprint/tla-card-records-keep-every-field-across-language-hops.w1.g2.e19 (CardHops.tla and five cfgs; the positive cfg exhausted green and each reversed cfg failed its named invariant; a reader accepted it); the landing refused it only on a tla/RUNS.tsv ledger conflict (the CardHops record appears twice), so attempt 2 was to rebase on the base tip and resolve the ledger. Resume from that head; do not start over. Stream branch: sprint/schema-vt-core (base sprint/schema-finish).")
  (:id "cards/the-card-corpus-is-a-language-neutral-conformance-set" :type :task :title "The card corpus is a language-neutral conformance set" :state :done :evidence ("test/conformance/harness/cards_test.go: TestCardsCheckComparesEverySurface, TestCardsCheckRefusesARequiredAbsence (RUN and PASS, an in-process fake driver, no subprocess)" "make cards-conformance-go (cards <surface> pass n/m for all nine surfaces with no absence) and make cards-conformance-negative-control (one render and one taskhash answer byte changed, exactly those two surfaces red)") :sprint-card "the-card-corpus-is-a-language-neutral-conformance-set" :sprint-column "waiting" :sprint-stream "schema-vt-core" :sprint-base "sprint/schema-vt-core" :tier "pro" :needs ("schema-cards-c04-field-edits-and-the-view" "tla-card-records-keep-every-field-across-language-hops") :note "Saved from the sprint store on 2026-10-12 (epoch 19) before the clear; not landed. Task: a language-neutral card conformance set under tables/cards/conformance, a Go reference driver that writes its expected answers, and a cards subcommand of the existing conformance harness that runs any language driver over it and compares bytes; the checker cites tla/CardHops.tla (ImplementationsAgree, HopOrderIrrelevant). Done when make cards-conformance-go passes with every surface required, the negative control goes red on a one-byte change, and TestCardsCheckComparesEverySurface and TestCardsCheckRefusesARequiredAbsence pass. Needs: schema-cards-c04-field-edits-and-the-view (landed), tla-card-records-keep-every-field-across-language-hops (open, work pushed). Order: first in line in schema-vt-core; needed by every a-<lang>-card-round-trips-and-renders-the-shared-corpus card and by the-cards-page-and-roadmap-name-every-language. No attempt was dealt; nothing pushed. Stream branch: sprint/schema-vt-core (base sprint/schema-finish).")
  (:id "cards/the-cards-page-and-roadmap-name-every-language" :type :task :title "The cards page and the roadmap name every language" :state :todo :evidence nil :sprint-card "the-cards-page-and-roadmap-name-every-language" :sprint-column "waiting" :sprint-stream "schema-vt-core" :sprint-base "sprint/schema-vt-core" :tier "pro" :needs ("schema-cards-c05-the-cards-page" "the-card-corpus-is-a-language-neutral-conformance-set" "a-c-card-upgrades-edits-and-walks-the-shared-corpus" "a-cpp-card-upgrades-edits-and-walks-the-shared-corpus" "a-cs-card-upgrades-edits-and-walks-the-shared-corpus" "a-rust-card-upgrades-edits-and-walks-the-shared-corpus" "a-java-card-upgrades-edits-and-walks-the-shared-corpus" "a-js-card-upgrades-edits-and-walks-the-shared-corpus" "a-dart-card-upgrades-edits-and-walks-the-shared-corpus" "a-elixir-card-upgrades-edits-and-walks-the-shared-corpus") :note "Saved from the sprint store on 2026-10-12 (epoch 19) before the clear; not landed. Task: one make target (cards-conformance-all) proves all nine legs on all nine card conformance surfaces, docs/CARDS.md teaches every leg (generate, the facade calls in that language mapped to the Go names, bounds, retention limits, the make targets, the two models), TestCardsPageNamesEveryLanguage fails when a language section or facade call is removed, and the ROADMAP.md Future table gains the card rows marked only for the legs whose check passed in this card gate; docs/PORTING.md gains the card techniques per language. Needs: schema-cards-c05-the-cards-page (landed), the-card-corpus-is-a-language-neutral-conformance-set (open), and every a-<lang>-card-upgrades-edits-and-walks-the-shared-corpus card for c, cpp, cs, rust, java, js, dart, elixir (all open). Order: last of three in schema-vt-core; the closing card of the whole variable-tables chain. No attempt was dealt; nothing pushed. Stream branch: sprint/schema-vt-core (base sprint/schema-finish).")
  (:id "schema-vt-core" :type :work-set :title "Cards as variable tables: the shared model, corpus and page (sprint stream schema-vt-core)" :note "The language-neutral core of the card variable-table work: the cross-language TLA+ model, the shared conformance corpus with its Go answers and harness subcommand, and the closing page-and-roadmap card. Stream branch sprint/schema-vt-core, cut from sprint/schema-finish; its cards land on it in a batch (oldest first) and the stream branch merges serially into sprint/schema-finish. Order in the stream: the-card-corpus-is-a-language-neutral-conformance-set, tla-card-records-keep-every-field-across-language-hops (which the corpus needs), the-cards-page-and-roadmap-name-every-language." :origin "cards from the sprint store (2026-10-12, epoch 19)" :children ("cards/the-card-corpus-is-a-language-neutral-conformance-set" "cards/tla-card-records-keep-every-field-across-language-hops" "cards/the-cards-page-and-roadmap-name-every-language"))
  (:id "cards/a-c-card-round-trips-and-renders-the-shared-corpus" :type :task :title "Layers L1 and L2 of the card design in C: round-trip and render the shared corpus" :state :todo :evidence nil :sprint-card "a-c-card-round-trips-and-renders-the-shared-corpus" :sprint-column "waiting" :sprint-stream "schema-vt-c" :sprint-base "sprint/schema-vt-c" :tier "pro" :needs ("the-card-corpus-is-a-language-neutral-conformance-set") :note "Saved from the sprint store on 2026-10-12 (epoch 19) before the clear; not landed. Task: layers L1 and L2 of the card design in C: the card record as a generated variable table with an owning facade and the customer bounds, and the brief text parsed once and rendered many times, each matching the Go leg byte for byte on the shared corpus. The facade lives in tables/cards/c (cards.h, cards.c, sha256.c, cards_test.c, driver.c and the executable driver script); its calls are the Go facade calls in the language's own spelling. Done when make cards-c-test runs TestCardRoundTripsThePopulatedFixture, TestCardBoundsRefuseBeforePublishing and TestParseRenderMatchesGo green, make cards-c-conformance reports pass for load, save, render, parse and bounds, and the negative control goes red on render only. Needs: the-card-corpus-is-a-language-neutral-conformance-set (open). Order: first in line in schema-vt-c; needed by a-c-card-upgrades-edits-and-walks-the-shared-corpus. No attempt was dealt; nothing pushed. Stream branch: sprint/schema-vt-c (base sprint/schema-finish).")
  (:id "cards/a-c-card-upgrades-edits-and-walks-the-shared-corpus" :type :task :title "Layers L3 and L4 of the card design in C: upgrade, edit and walk the shared corpus" :state :todo :evidence nil :sprint-card "a-c-card-upgrades-edits-and-walks-the-shared-corpus" :sprint-column "waiting" :sprint-stream "schema-vt-c" :sprint-base "sprint/schema-vt-c" :tier "pro" :needs ("a-c-card-round-trips-and-renders-the-shared-corpus") :note "Saved from the sprint store on 2026-10-12 (epoch 19) before the clear; not landed. Task: layers L3 and L4 of the card design in C: an old card upgraded to the current declaration losing nothing, field edits that leave the body and the task hash alone, and the view that walks a record by name and kind, each matching the Go leg on the shared corpus; each function cites the property it keeps from tla/CardVersioning.tla (NoFieldLost, BodyUnchanged, RefusalKeepsOriginal) and tla/CardHops.tla (ImplementationsAgree, TaskHashStable, the reversed witness EditDropsUnknown). Done when make cards-c-test runs TestUpgradeMatchesGo, TestTaskHashFramesLogicalFields, TestFieldEditLeavesTheTaskHashAlone and TestViewWalksEveryField green, make cards-c-conformance requires and passes all nine surfaces with no absence, and the upgrade and hash negative controls each go red on their own surface only. Needs: a-c-card-round-trips-and-renders-the-shared-corpus (open). Order: second of two in schema-vt-c, after a-c-card-round-trips-and-renders-the-shared-corpus; needed by the-cards-page-and-roadmap-name-every-language. No attempt was dealt; nothing pushed. Stream branch: sprint/schema-vt-c (base sprint/schema-finish).")
