  (:id "card-variable-tables" :type :work-set :title "Cards as variable tables in every language: planned work saved from sprint epoch 19 (2026-10-12)" :note "Saved from the sprint store on 2026-10-12, epoch 19, before the clear: the 19 open cards of the card variable-table work, one task per card, each :todo (one :doing, whose pushed head is cited in its node) with the card id, its column at the save, its stream, its base branch, its needs and the stream order in its note. Landed cards of these streams are not listed; they are in git on sprint/schema-finish and the sprint/schema-vt-* branches. The streams schema-finish and schema-cards had every card landed at the save and contribute nothing here. THE LANDING FLOW: each stream lands its cards in a batch (oldest first) onto its own branch sprint/<stream>, and the stream branches merge serially into sprint/schema-finish, the schema integration branch. Dependency order across streams: schema-vt-core first (tla-card-records-keep-every-field-across-language-hops, then the-card-corpus-is-a-language-neutral-conformance-set), then the eight language streams in parallel (round-trips before upgrades in each), then the-cards-page-and-roadmap-name-every-language closes the chain. The card record is a Future row of the page, outside the NEW Fixed Tables denominators; these tasks are not cells of the fixed-tables table." :origin "cards from the sprint store (2026-10-12, epoch 19)" :children ("schema-vt-core" "schema-vt-c" "schema-vt-cpp" "schema-vt-cs" "schema-vt-rust" "schema-vt-java" "schema-vt-js" "schema-vt-dart" "schema-vt-elixir"))
  ; The packet-wire roadmap: one task per language and gate, the evidence the legs' make targets.
  (:id "packet-wire" :type :roadmap :title "Packet wire" :text ("Constants, enums, flags and types: bit-packed structs exchanged between client and server with exactly the same protocol version." "A cell is ✅ when the language's packet leg passes on this branch: the examples generated and run against the shared wire vectors the C++ reference writes (make test-<lang>), with the packet-text (#519), packet-wide (#188) and packet-defaults (#396) gates and their negative controls.") :rows (("constants" "constants and compile-time expressions") ("enums" "enums") ("flags" "flags") ("types" "types, bitpacked structs") ("composition" "composition of types by value") ("unions" "tagged unions of type payloads") ("payload-free-arms" "named payload-free union arms") ("bool" "bool") ("full-width-integers" "full-width integers, 8 to 64 bits") ("ranged-integers" "ranged integers") ("bits" "bits(N)") ("int128" "raw uint128 and ranged int128") ("floats" "raw float32 and float64") ("compressed-float" "compressed float32") ("fixed-point" "fixed(I, F) and ufixed(I, F)") ("bytes" "bytes(N)") ("string" "string(N)") ("string-utf8-refusal" "string(N) refuses malformed UTF-8 on read (#519)") ("wstring" "wstring(N) (#188)") ("fixed-arrays" "fixed arrays [N]T") ("counted-arrays" "counted arrays [A..B]T") ("if-else" "if / else") ("const" "on-wire const(Value, Bits)") ("reserved" "reserved(Bits)") ("align" "align") ("scalar-defaults" "defaults for scalar, enum and fixed fields") ("text-defaults" "string, bytes and flags defaults (#396)") ("protocol-id" "the protocol id")) :columns (("cpp" "cpp") ("c" "c") ("cs" "cs") ("go" "go") ("rust" "rust") ("java" "java") ("js" "js") ("dart" "dart") ("elixir" "elixir")) :cells (("constants" "cpp" "packet/cpp/leg") ("constants" "c" "packet/c/leg") ("constants" "cs" "packet/cs/leg") ("constants" "go" "packet/go/leg") ("constants" "rust" "packet/rust/leg") ("constants" "java" "packet/java/leg") ("constants" "js" "packet/js/leg") ("constants" "dart" "packet/dar