  (:id "vt/c/generator-panic" :type :task :title "C: a red at the branch head that holds 31 cells" :state :todo :evidence nil :tested-revision "6410065dc" :note "RED ONE STEP ON: the R2.schema nil-arm panic is fixed (internal/codegen/ctable/fixedform.go fixedCollectTypes and the union-arm writer; TestGenerateR2DoesNotPanic green) and ./bin/schema generate --lang c test/tables/R2.schema exits 0, but make tables-c is still red at a second, pre-existing C fixed-form gap: the union-arm writer calls emitFixedWriteElement on the arm directly, so a TEXT or wide-text arm is sized by ir.TableFixedStorageBytes as 0 and the generated body emits table_fixed_put0(..., (uint0_t) ...) — build/tables-generated-c/a2/A2Table.h:4212 (union Value, arm c string(8)), build/tables-generated-c/messages/MessagesTable.h:9925, build/tables-generated-c/wide/CaptionTable.h:4611 (union Body, arm wide wstring(4)). The C emitter needs an emitFixedWriteArm twin of the reference (internal/codegen/cpptable/fixedform.go:473) routing text, array and counted arms through emitFixedWritePayload; that is a new card. make tables-c also stops on build/tables-generated-c/scalars/ScalarsTable.h:32: fatal error: serialize.h: No such file or directory, because SERIALIZE_C defaults to ../serialize.c, absent in this worktree.")
