  (:id "vt/cs/generator-panic" :type :task :title "C#: a red at the branch head that holds 31 cells" :state :done :evidence ("internal/codegen/cstable/fixedform_csunions_test.go: TestGenerateCsUnionsDoesNotPanic, TestFixedArmLayoutMatchesReference, TestFixedArmWritesAreFieldLines" "./bin/schema generate --lang cs --out build/x test/tables/CsUnions.schema exits 0" "make tables-cs-leg, tables-cs-wire-fuzz, tables-cs-retain-fuzz, tables-cs-view, tables-cook-open-cs, tables-block, tables-block-fuzz") :tested-revision "8c6aaa9a7" :note "RUN green on the hetzner2 bench at 8c6aaa9a7 (Linux, the pinned toolchains): the unit tests, the generate command and every make target named (tables-block's TSan binary needs ASLR off on that 6.8 kernel, setarch -R, else TSan refuses with unexpected memory mapping before any test runs). Three reds stood in a row behind the generator. (1) A payload-free arm (empty in Leaf, signal in Choice) has a nil field, and fixedCollectTypes read v.F.Type at fixedform.go:181 (the write, slot and block walks the same): every arm walk now skips it as cpptable/fixedform.go:280-282 does (§2.6). (2) Every arm was walked as a bare element, so a string or bytes arm spelled csFieldType's fallback, (/* ? */)v in MessagesTable.cs, A2Table.cs and CaptionTable.cs, and an array arm was walked as one struct; the C# layout hash of every root holding such an arm, or a payload-free one, differed from the reference's (ir.TableFixedWalkRoot). An arm is a field line (§2.6): the block, slot, plan, write and bounds walks now take an arm through the payload walk with the union as owner, and a nested element loop takes its own counter (CS0136). (3) test/cs-tables FixedFormChecks.cs called TableFixedWire.Compile without the split added in 978f891ac; the emitted runtime gains the five-argument overload.")
