  (:id "vt/variable-class/js" :type :task :title "JavaScript: variable class (pointers, the flat node table)" :state :done :evidence ("internal/codegen/jstable/variableclass_test.go TestVariableClassBeyondCardConstructsJavaScript: table pointers *T over the flat node table (tables/pointers graph_tree, graph_shared, graph_empty, graph_deep, a shared node one object after the load), tables nested by value, bounded arrays of tables, and the rest of the scalar kinds (uint8..uint64, int8, int16 with a range, float32, float64, bits(N), bool) with declared defaults in the classprobe unit; make tables-js-variable-class (in make test-js)" "internal/codegen/jstable/cardsform_test.go TestOtherVariableConstructsAreRefusedByName: what the leg still refuses, by name" "test/conformance/js/main.mjs: surfaceWire, surfaceReport for graphdemo Scene and blobdemo Catalog (./build/conformance-harness run --only js: make conformance is red on head and base alike, the C generator panics at make/c.mk:119)") :tested-revision "de33b2a91" :note "RUN at de33b2a91 plus this change, on the Linux bench b1: the test and the make target named here passed, every case byte for byte against the Go oracle (internal/tablewire, internal/tabletext). The walk is one descriptor-driven port of the oracle (internal/codegen/jstable/variableruntime.go). A node is numbered by object identity; a data cycle refuses the save (null). Retention inside a node record is not kept (it counts retainLost): vt/retain-unknown/js.")
  (:id "vt/text-form-variable/js" :type :task :title "JavaScript: text form, variable class" :state :done :evidence ("internal/codegen/jstable/variableclass_test.go TestVariableClassBeyondCardConstructsJavaScript: json write and json read of every pointered, blob and list instance with a text, the &node definition and reference (graph_shared, list_tables, list_shared, list_before_pointer, classprobe probe_full), and the writer's refusal of a blob two slots name (blob_shared, probe_shared_string); make tables-js-variable-class (in make test-js)" "internal/codegen/jstable/cardsform_test.go TestCardTextFormMatchesGo" "test/conformance/js/main.mjs: surfaceJsonRead, surfaceJsonWrite (./build/conformance-harness run --only js)") :tested-revision "de33b2a91" :note "RUN at de33b2a91 plus this change, on the Linux bench b1: the test and the make target named here passed, every case byte for byte against the Go oracle. The text reader is a port of internal/tabletext read.go (comments, trailing commas, &node labels, a definition inside a skipped value keeps its label); the json-hostile battery is not this leg's surface yet.")
