  (:id "vt/blobs/js" :type :task :title "JavaScript: blobs (*bytes, *string)" :state :done :evidence ("internal/codegen/jstable/variableclass_test.go TestVariableClassBeyondCardConstructsJavaScript: *bytes and *string blobs, empty, large and shared (tables/blobs blob_small, blob_empty, blob_large, blob_shared, blob_str8, blob_str16), two equal blobs in two slots as two records (probe_equal_strings, probe_empty_strings, probe_equal_bytes, probe_empty_bytes) and one *string two slots share as one (probe_shared_string); make tables-js-variable-class (in make test-js)" "compiler/target_javascript.go: registerBuiltin with blobs=true; compiler/tablescs_test.go TestCsCarriesBlobs names js a carrier" "test/conformance/js/main.mjs: blobdemo Catalog on the wire and text surfaces (./build/conformance-harness run --only js)") :tested-revision "de33b2a91" :note "RUN at de33b2a91 plus this change, on the Linux bench b1: the test and the make target named here passed, every case byte for byte against the Go oracle. A blob is numbered by OBJECT identity as the oracle numbers it: a Uint8Array is an object, a *string held as a primitive is its own record per slot, and a String object is the spelling of a *string two slots share (a load hands one to each slot that names a shared record).")
