  (:id "sprint-out/js-base-forward-merge-schema-go" :type :task :title "sprint/schema-js takes sprint/schema-go: the JavaScript base forward-merge" :state :todo :evidence nil :sprint-card "js-base-forward-merge-schema-go" :sprint-column "review" :sprint-stream "schema-js" :sprint-base "sprint/schema-js" :tier "heavy" :needs "none" :pushed-head "77797d187023be292bede4f9bce409b5bcc07e52" :pushed-branch "sprint/js-base-forward-merge-schema-go.w3.g1.e21" :note "Carried: branch sprint/js-base-forward-merge-schema-go.w3.g1.e21 head 77797d187023be292bede4f9bce409b5bcc07e52 (attempt 6, review). Task: sprint/schema-js takes sprint/schema-go: the JavaScript base forward-merge. Moved out of the sprint on 2026-10-19 (Glenn: \"Please take all work in the current sprint that is not for this rocketnet release and push it out to the appropriate roadmap sexp\"): sprint card js-base-forward-merge-schema-go of stream schema-js was in review, not landed; the card was dropped from the sprint naming this item, and its pushed head stays on that branch. :brief-file holds the card's whole brief at the move." :task "THE TASK. sprint/schema-js is about 686 commits behind sprint/schema-go (64dc1ddd when carded; GO TIP below is the tip you fetch, at or after it). Merge origin/sprint/schema-go into the base as ONE merge commit on the card branch: git fetch origin, then git merge --no-ff GO TIP. Never a rebase, never a squash, never a force-push. A trial merge on 2026-10-18 left these conflicts (a newer GO TIP may add a few; resolve those by the same rules): ROADMAP.md, docs/roadmap.sexp, internal/codegen/jstable/fixedruntime.go. Resolve each conflict keeping BOTH sides' intent, by these rules and no others: shared Go and IR code (ir/, internal/check/, internal/parser/, compiler/, internal/codegen/gotable/, tools/, .github/) takes GO TIP's version; port-specific code keeps the port's version, adapted to the new IR; spec text (docs/*.md) merges both rewrites, each statement true of the merged code; ROADMAP.md is regenerated with make roadmap, never hand-edited; the roadmap sexp ledgers (docs/roadmap.sexp, docs/roadmap-evidence/*.sexp) keep each row's true state at the merge head. jstable/fixedruntime.go is port-specific: keep the JS base's behaviour, adapted to the IR GO TIP carries; the JS fixed-fo [...]" :brief-file "docs/roadmap-briefs/schema-cards-out-2026-10-19.sexp")
  (:id "sprint-out/js-blob-named-twice-is-refused-by-every-writer" :type :task :title "JavaScript: one blob named from two slots is written by no writer, counted by the tolerant read and refused by the strict read" :state :todo :evidence nil :sprint-card "js-blob-named-twice-is-refused-by-every-writer" :sprint-column "waiting" :sprint-stream "schema-js" :sprint-base "sprint/schema-js" :tier "pro" :needs "js-base-forward-merge-schema-go,js-plain-variable-load-is-strict" :pushed-head "" :pushed-branch "" :note "Waiting card js-blob-named-twice-is-refused-by-every-writer of stream schema-js, deferred out of the sprint on 2026-10-19 (Glenn: not for the rocketnet v1.0.0 release; moved to the roadmap) with nova-sprint defer; not started in the sprint. :brief-file holds the card's whole brief as defer wrote it." :task "THE RULE. docs/SPEC-TABLES.md §2.5 (\"A blob is OWNED BY ONE SLOT\"), §6.5 (blob_shared), §16.7: every writer refuses to emit a wire where two slots name one blob record (Measure -1 and Save null with reason blob_shared; the text writer refuses the graph); the TOLERANT read keeps the value with both slots naming the one node it decoded and counts each extra naming in a `blobShared` counter; the STRICT read refuses `blob_shared`. Oracle: internal/codegen/gotable/blobnamedtwice_test.go (TestBlobNamedTwiceSeed24, TestBlobNamedTwiceWriters, TestBlobNamedTwiceAmplification)." :brief-file "docs/roadmap-briefs/schema-cards-out-2026-10-19.sexp")
  (:id "sprint-out/js-block-carries-the-wide-kinds" :type :task :title "JavaScript's block form carries the wide kinds: 128-bit integers and fixed point" :state :todo :evidence nil :sprint-card "js-block-carries-the-wide-kinds" :sprint-column "waiting" :sprint-stream "schema-js" :sprint-base "sprint/schema-js" :tier "pro" :needs "js-base-forward-merge-schema-go" :pushed-head "" :pushed-branch "" :note "Waiting card js-block-carries-the-wide-kinds of stream schema-js, deferred out of the sprint on 2026-10-19 (Glenn: not for the rocketnet v1.0.0 release; moved to the roadmap) with nova-sprint defer; not started in the sprint. :brief-file holds the card's whole brief as defer wrote it." :task "THE RULE. docs/SPEC-TABLES.md §19 (the block form) and §15's wide kinds: Go's block form lays out and reads `int128`/`uint128` and `fixed(I, F)` fields; ir.WideTableKinds (ir/tablekind.go) is the scope rule for a port that does not carry them yet. Oracle: internal/codegen/gotable/block.go and blockbuild.go at d808c3f54 (the Go block image of the same declaration)." :brief-file "docs/roadmap-briefs/schema-cards-out-2026-10-19.sexp")
  (:id "sprint-out/js-carries-bounded-text-lists" :type :task :title "JavaScript carries bounded text lists: `[N]string(M)`, `[E]string(M)`, `[..N]string(M)` and `[..N]?string(M)`" :state :todo :evidence nil :sprint-card "js-carries-bounded-text-lists" :sprint-column "waiting" :sprint-stream "schema-js" :sprint-base "sprint/schema-js" :tier "pro" :needs "js-base-forward-merge-schema-go,schema-go-target-names-what-it-carries" :pushed-head "" :pushed-branch "" :note "Waiting card js-carries-bounded-text-lists of stream schema-js, deferred out of the sprint on 2026-10-19 (Glenn: not for the rocketnet v1.0.0 release; moved to the roadmap) with nova-sprint defer; not started in the sprint. :brief-file holds the card's whole brief as defer wrote it." :task "THE RULE. docs/SPEC-TABLES.md §2.13 \"Text lists: `rules [..16]string(64)`\": a list of text is COUNTED; its wire, its storage, its fixed-form layout where the class allows, and its JSON spelling, as §2.13 states and Go's generated code does. Oracle: internal/codegen/gotable/stringarrays_test.go TestGoTableStringArraysAndJSONArrayRoot (the text-list half; the array root is js-carries-the-json-array-root)." :brief-file "docs/roadmap-briefs/schema-cards-out-2026-10-19.sexp")
  (:id "sprint-out/js-carries-integrity-on-the-fixed-and-message-forms" :type :task :title "JavaScript carries the integrity trailer on the fixed form (once per form-3 file) and the message form (once per batch)" :state :todo :evidence nil :sprint-card "js-carries-integrity-on-the-fixed-and-message-forms" :sprint-column "waiting" :sprint-stream "schema-js" :sprint-base "sprint/schema-js" :tier "pro" :needs "js-base-forward-merge-schema-go,schema-go-target-names-what-it-carries,js-carries-integrity-on-the-variable-wire" :pushed-head "" :pushed-branch "" :note "Waiting card js-carries-integrity-on-the-fixed-and-message-forms of stream schema-js, deferred out of the sprint on 2026-10-19 (Glenn: not for the rocketnet v1.0.0 release; moved to the roadmap) with nova-sprint defer; not started in the sprint. :brief-file holds the card's whole brief as defer wrote it." :task "THE RULE. docs/SPEC-TABLES.md §2.14, §3.4 and §3.3: a fixed table's form-3 file carries the CRC-32C trailer once per file and its message-form batch once per batch, checked before any record decodes, missing or mismatched refused by name. Oracle: internal/codegen/gotable/integrity_test.go TestGoWireIntegrityCheckFixedForm and TestGoWireIntegrityCheckMessageForm." :brief-file "docs/roadmap-briefs/schema-cards-out-2026-10-19.sexp")
  (:id "sprint-out/js-carries-integrity-on-the-variable-wire" :type :task :title "JavaScript carries `integrity = \"crc32c\"` on the variable-form file: the CRC-32C trailer written and checked" :state :todo :evidence nil :sprint-card "js-carries-integrity-on-the-variable-wire" :sprint-column "waiting" :sprint-stream "schema-js" :sprint-base "sprint/schema-js" :tier "pro" :needs "js-base-forward-merge-schema-go,schema-go-target-names-what-it-carries,js-savetext-loadtext-carry-canonical-base64" :pushed-head "" :pushed-branch "" :note "Waiting card js-carries-integrity-on-the-variable-wire of stream schema-js, deferred out of the sprint on 2026-10-19 (Glenn: not for the rocketnet v1.0.0 release; moved to the roadmap) with nova-sprint defer; not started in the sprint. :brief-file holds the card's whole brief as defer wrote it." :task "THE RULE. docs/SPEC-TABLES.md §2.14 \"The integrity check: `integrity`\" and §3: a table declaring `integrity = \"crc32c\"` saves its variable-form file with a CRC-32C trailer, every read checks it before decoding any field, a missing or mismatched trailer refuses by name, and a table without the key writes exactly the bytes it wrote before. Oracle: internal/codegen/gotable/integrity_test.go TestGoWireIntegrityCheck (no single-bit flip of any byte decodes as a value)." :brief-file "docs/roadmap-briefs/schema-cards-out-2026-10-19.sexp")
  (:id "sprint-out/js-carries-one-sided-integer-ranges" :type :task :title "JavaScript carries a one-sided integer range (`| min` alone or `| max` alone)" :state :todo :evidence nil :sprint-card "js-carries-one-sided-integer-ranges" :sprint-column "waiting" :sprint-stream "schema-js" :sprint-base "sprint/schema-js" :tier "pro" :needs "js-base-forward-merge-schema-go,schema-go-target-names-what-it-carries" :pushed-head "" :pushed-branch "" :note "Waiting card js-carries-one-sided-integer-ranges of stream schema-js, deferred out of the sprint on 2026-10-19 (Glenn: not for the rocketnet v1.0.0 release; moved to the roadmap) with nova-sprint defer; not started in the sprint. :brief-file holds the card's whole brief as defer wrote it." :task "THE RULE. docs/SPEC-TABLES.md §4.3 \"One-sided integer ranges\" and SPEC §4.6: `int64 | min = 0` and `uint16 | max = 9` clamp on the declared side only, every form, as Go's generated code does. Oracle: internal/check/onesided_test.go TestOneSidedIntegerRange and the Go leg's generated clamp." :brief-file "docs/roadmap-briefs/schema-cards-out-2026-10-19.sexp")
  (:id "sprint-out/js-carries-optional-maps" :type :task :title "JavaScript carries the optional map `?map[K]V`: absent, present-empty and present-with-entries are three values" :state :todo :evidence nil :sprint-card "js-carries-optional-maps" :sprint-column "waiting" :sprint-stream "schema-js" :sprint-base "sprint/schema-js" :tier "pro" :needs "js-base-forward-merge-schema-go,schema-go-target-names-what-it-carries" :pushed-head "" :pushed-branch "" :note "Waiting card js-carries-optional-maps of stream schema-js, deferred out of the sprint on 2026-10-19 (Glenn: not for the rocketnet v1.0.0 release; moved to the roadmap) with nova-sprint defer; not started in the sprint. :brief-file holds the card's whole brief as defer wrote it." :task "THE RULE. docs/SPEC-TABLES.md §2.8 read through §2.3: `tags ?map[string(8)]int32` carries a presence companion; ABSENT writes nothing, PRESENT-EMPTY writes the field header and the two-byte body `0d 00` under L = 2, present-with-entries is the plain map's bytes; JSON absent omits the key, present-empty is `{}`, `null` reads absent; retain-unknown and the cooked form keep the presence; the view names the field optional; a reader built without the `?` reads the three wires silently as the plain map. Oracle: internal/codegen/gotable/mappresence_test.go TestGoMapPresence." :brief-file "docs/roadmap-briefs/schema-cards-out-2026-10-19.sexp")
  (:id "sprint-out/js-carries-optional-over-a-variable-closure" :type :task :title "JavaScript carries `?T` whose T holds a pointer: every edge walk gates on presence" :state :todo :evidence nil :sprint-card "js-carries-optional-over-a-variable-closure" :sprint-column "waiting" :sprint-stream "schema-js" :sprint-base "sprint/schema-js" :tier "pro" :needs "js-base-forward-merge-schema-go,schema-go-target-names-what-it-carries" :pushed-head "" :pushed-branch "" :note "Waiting card js-carries-optional-over-a-variable-closure of stream schema-js, deferred out of the sprint on 2026-10-19 (Glenn: not for the rocketnet v1.0.0 release; moved to the roadmap) with nova-sprint defer; not started in the sprint. :brief-file holds the card's whole brief as defer wrote it." :task "THE RULE. docs/SPEC-TABLES.md §2.3: for `?T` over a variable closure every walk that follows pointer edges visits T's edges only when the presence companion is set, and an absent value owns no node; absent, present-with-text and present-empty round-trip the wire, base64 and JSON; a present value then cleared and saved writes no stale node through save, measure, the retaining save, the cook and the JSON writer. Oracle: internal/codegen/gotable/optionalvariable_test.go TestGoOptionalVariableClosureTable." :brief-file "docs/roadmap-briefs/schema-cards-out-2026-10-19.sexp")
  (:id "sprint-out/js-carries-required-in-the-text-form" :type :task :title "JavaScript's JSON text form honours `| required`: always written, a missing one refuses FromJson" :state :todo :evidence nil :sprint-card "js-carries-required-in-the-text-form" :sprint-column "waiting" :sprint-stream "schema-js" :sprint-base "sprint/schema-js" :tier "pro" :needs "js-base-forward-merge-schema-go,js-carries-required-on-the-wire" :pushed-head "" :pushed-branch "" :note "Waiting card js-carries-required-in-the-text-form of stream schema-js, deferred out of the sprint on 2026-10-19 (Glenn: not for the rocketnet v1.0.0 release; moved to the roadmap) with nova-sprint defer; not started in the sprint. :brief-file holds the card's whole brief as defer wrote it." :task "THE RULE. docs/SPEC-TABLES.md §6.5 (\"The text read counts a missing required field as the binary read does\") and §16.2 (omit-defaults writes a required field): a JSON object that leaves a `| required` field out counts missing_required once, naming the fields, so the plain FromJson refuses it and FromJsonTolerant answers false with the count; a required field off its branch is not demanded; ToJson under omit-defaults writes every required field. Oracle: the JSON legs of TestGoRequiredInOffBranch and TestGoDefaultReadIsStrict." :brief-file "docs/roadmap-briefs/schema-cards-out-2026-10-19.sexp")
  (:id "sprint-out/js-carries-required-on-the-wire" :type :task :title "JavaScript carries `| required` on the variable and message wires: written always, demanded on read, off-branch not demanded" :state :todo :evidence nil :sprint-card "js-carries-required-on-the-wire" :sprint-column "waiting" :sprint-stream "schema-js" :sprint-base "sprint/schema-js" :tier "pro" :needs "js-base-forward-merge-schema-go,schema-go-target-names-what-it-carries,js-plain-variable-load-is-strict" :pushed-head "" :pushed-branch "" :note "Waiting card js-carries-required-on-the-wire of stream schema-js, deferred out of the sprint on 2026-10-19 (Glenn: not for the rocketnet v1.0.0 release; moved to the roadmap) with nova-sprint defer; not started in the sprint. :brief-file holds the card's whole brief as defer wrote it." :task "THE RULE. docs/SPEC-TABLES.md §2.3 \"The `| required` marker\": a required field always rides (omit-defaults never elides it, §16.2), has no declared default, and a read that does not find it counts `missing_required` once, naming the field, at any depth, refusing the WHOLE record (136191a69); the strict read refuses it with missing_required. A required field inside a guard/union arm that is OFF is absent from the wire and not demanded; with the branch on it must ride. Oracles: internal/codegen/gotable/requiredoffbranch_test.go TestGoRequiredInOffBranch, internal/codegen/gotable/requirednodefault_test.go TestGoRequiredExactFieldHasNoDefault, and the missing_required cases of TestGoDefaultReadIsStrict." :brief-file "docs/roadmap-briefs/schema-cards-out-2026-10-19.sexp")
  (:id "sprint-out/js-carries-retain-in-the-message-form" :type :task :title "JavaScript carries retain-unknown in the message form: LoadRetainMessages and its save" :state :todo :evidence nil :sprint-card "js-carries-retain-in-the-message-form" :sprint-column "waiting" :sprint-stream "schema-js" :sprint-base "sprint/schema-js" :tier "pro" :needs "js-base-forward-merge-schema-go" :pushed-head "" :pushed-branch "" :note "Waiting card js-carries-retain-in-the-message-form of stream schema-js, deferred out of the sprint on 2026-10-19 (Glenn: not for the rocketnet v1.0.0 release; moved to the roadmap) with nova-sprint defer; not started in the sprint. :brief-file holds the card's whole brief as defer wrote it." :task "THE RULE. docs/SPEC-TABLES.md §6.6 \"Retain-unknown\": the retain family covers the message form too (`LoadRetainMessages`, §6.5's list), keeping what this build cannot name per record and writing it back. Oracle: internal/codegen/gotable/retainmessage.go and its tests (internal/codegen/gotable, grep LoadRetainMessages)." :brief-file "docs/roadmap-briefs/schema-cards-out-2026-10-19.sexp")
  (:id "sprint-out/js-carries-text-list-total-bytes" :type :task :title "JavaScript carries a text list's `| total = N` byte bound on every writer and reader" :state :todo :evidence nil :sprint-card "js-carries-text-list-total-bytes" :sprint-column "waiting" :sprint-stream "schema-js" :sprint-base "sprint/schema-js" :tier "pro" :needs "js-base-forward-merge-schema-go,schema-go-target-names-what-it-carries,js-carries-unbounded-text" :pushed-head "" :pushed-branch "" :note "Waiting card js-carries-text-list-total-bytes of stream schema-js, deferred out of the sprint on 2026-10-19 (Glenn: not for the rocketnet v1.0.0 release; moved to the roadmap) with nova-sprint defer; not started in the sprint. :brief-file holds the card's whole brief as defer wrote it." :task "THE RULE. docs/SPEC-TABLES.md §2.13 (the TOTAL): `| total = N` bounds the sum of a text list's element bytes; writers refuse a value past it (Save and Measure -1, ToJsonMeasure -1, the retaining save -1); readers keep the longest prefix within the total, drop the rest, count clamped once naming the field, and the strict read refuses clamped. Oracle: internal/codegen/gotable/listtotalbytes_test.go TestGoTextListTotalBytesBound (all four spellings)." :brief-file "docs/roadmap-briefs/schema-cards-out-2026-10-19.sexp")
  (:id "sprint-out/js-carries-the-forms-declaration" :type :task :title "JavaScript honours a table's `forms` declaration: it emits exactly the forms the table names" :state :todo :evidence nil :sprint-card "js-carries-the-forms-declaration" :sprint-column "waiting" :sprint-stream "schema-js" :sprint-base "sprint/schema-js" :tier "pro" :needs "js-base-forward-merge-schema-go,schema-go-target-names-what-it-carries" :pushed-head "" :pushed-branch "" :note "Waiting card js-carries-the-forms-declaration of stream schema-js, deferred out of the sprint on 2026-10-19 (Glenn: not for the rocketnet v1.0.0 release; moved to the roadmap) with nova-sprint defer; not started in the sprint. :brief-file holds the card's whole brief as defer wrote it." :task "THE RULE. docs/SPEC-TABLES.md §2.12 \"The forms a table carries: `forms`\": a table's explicit forms list decides which forms (wire, json, fixed, message, cook, block, ...) the generator emits for it, as Go does; a missing form's surface is absent, and a request §2.12 refuses is refused by name. Oracle: the Go leg's generated surface for the same declarations (internal/codegen/gotable, grep DeclaredForms)." :brief-file "docs/roadmap-briefs/schema-cards-out-2026-10-19.sexp")
  (:id "sprint-out/js-carries-the-hand-editable-text-form-read" :type :task :title "JavaScript reads the hand-editable text form (§16.9) into a table value, strictly" :state :todo :evidence nil :sprint-card "js-carries-the-hand-editable-text-form-read" :sprint-column "waiting" :sprint-stream "schema-js" :sprint-base "sprint/schema-js" :tier "pro" :needs "js-base-forward-merge-schema-go" :pushed-head "" :pushed-branch "" :note "Waiting card js-carries-the-hand-editable-text-form-read of stream schema-js, deferred out of the sprint on 2026-10-19 (Glenn: not for the rocketnet v1.0.0 release; moved to the roadmap) with nova-sprint defer; not started in the sprint. :brief-file holds the card's whole brief as defer wrote it." :task "THE RULE. docs/SPEC-TABLES.md §16.9 (16.9.1 grammar and identity, 16.9.2 mapping, 16.9.4 named refusals): a strict s-expression authoring form for fixed and variable tables, selected by the caller, every value resolved against the field's kind, no clamping, truncation, unknown-key skipping or last-wins, absent fields at their defaults, refusals by name (text_syntax, text_inactive_field and the rest). Oracle: internal/codegen/gotable/textform.go (Go's generated <Base>TableTextForm) and test/conformance/textform (inputs, values and the refusals/*.sexp with their .reason)." :brief-file "docs/roadmap-briefs/schema-cards-out-2026-10-19.sexp")
  (:id "sprint-out/js-carries-the-hand-editable-text-form-write" :type :task :title "JavaScript writes the hand-editable text form and edits it losslessly (§16.9.3)" :state :todo :evidence nil :sprint-card "js-carries-the-hand-editable-text-form-write" :sprint-column "waiting" :sprint-stream "schema-js" :sprint-base "sprint/schema-js" :tier "pro" :needs "js-base-forward-merge-schema-go,js-carries-the-hand-editable-text-form-read" :pushed-head "" :pushed-branch "" :note "Waiting card js-carries-the-hand-editable-text-form-write of stream schema-js, deferred out of the sprint on 2026-10-19 (Glenn: not for the rocketnet v1.0.0 release; moved to the roadmap) with nova-sprint defer; not started in the sprint. :brief-file holds the card's whole brief as defer wrote it." :task "THE RULE. docs/SPEC-TABLES.md §16.9.3 \"Comments, layout and lossless edits\": the document writer retains the source bytes, comments and layout, rewriting only what an edit changes; a fresh write uses the canonical layout. Oracle: internal/codegen/gotable/textform.go's writer and test/conformance/textform (*.rewrite.sexp, roadmap.edit.json, roadmap.edited.sexp)." :brief-file "docs/roadmap-briefs/schema-cards-out-2026-10-19.sexp")
  (:id "sprint-out/js-carries-the-json-array-root" :type :task :title "JavaScript carries the JSON array root: `table GoalList | json = \"array\"`" :state :todo :evidence nil :sprint-card "js-carries-the-json-array-root" :sprint-column "waiting" :sprint-stream "schema-js" :sprint-base "sprint/schema-js" :tier "pro" :needs "js-base-forward-merge-schema-go,schema-go-target-names-what-it-carries" :pushed-head "" :pushed-branch "" :note "Waiting card js-carries-the-json-array-root of stream schema-js, deferred out of the sprint on 2026-10-19 (Glenn: not for the rocketnet v1.0.0 release; moved to the roadmap) with nova-sprint defer; not started in the sprint. :brief-file holds the card's whole brief as defer wrote it." :task "THE RULE. docs/SPEC-TABLES.md §16.10 \"The array root\": a table whose one field is a list, declared `| json = \"array\"`, writes and reads its JSON text as a bare JSON array rather than an object; the binary wire is unchanged. Oracle: TestGoTableStringArraysAndJSONArrayRoot (the array-root half, internal/codegen/gotable/stringarrays_test.go)." :brief-file "docs/roadmap-briefs/schema-cards-out-2026-10-19.sexp")
  (:id "sprint-out/js-carries-timestamp-on-the-table-wires" :type :task :title "JavaScript carries the timestamp kind (kind 36) on the variable, fixed and message wires" :state :todo :evidence nil :sprint-card "js-carries-timestamp-on-the-table-wires" :sprint-column "waiting" :sprint-stream "schema-js" :sprint-base "sprint/schema-js" :tier "pro" :needs "js-base-forward-merge-schema-go,schema-go-target-names-what-it-carries" :pushed-head "" :pushed-branch "" :note "Waiting card js-carries-timestamp-on-the-table-wires of stream schema-js, deferred out of the sprint on 2026-10-19 (Glenn: not for the rocketnet v1.0.0 release; moved to the roadmap) with nova-sprint defer; not started in the sprint. :brief-file holds the card's whole brief as defer wrote it." :task "THE RULE. docs/SPEC-TABLES.md §2.11 \"Timestamps: `opened_at timestamp`\" and SPEC.md §4.13: the timestamp kind (table wire kind 36) and its storage and wire spelling as §2.11 states them. Go carries it first and every other target refuses it by name until its own turn (compiler/generate.go); scope widened 2026-10-18 (\"We do all features across all languages\"): this is the JS leg's turn. Oracle: the Go leg's generated code for a timestamp field (internal/codegen/gotable at d808c3f54) and test/conformance/harness/timestamp_kind_test.go." :brief-file "docs/roadmap-briefs/schema-cards-out-2026-10-19.sexp")
  (:id "sprint-out/js-carries-unbounded-text" :type :task :title "JavaScript carries unbounded text: `[]string`, `[]?string`, `[..N]string`, `[..N]?string` elements and `map[string]V` keys" :state :todo :evidence nil :sprint-card "js-carries-unbounded-text" :sprint-column "waiting" :sprint-stream "schema-js" :sprint-base "sprint/schema-js" :tier "pro" :needs "js-base-forward-merge-schema-go,schema-go-target-names-what-it-carries,js-carries-bounded-text-lists" :pushed-head "" :pushed-branch "" :note "Waiting card js-carries-unbounded-text of stream schema-js, deferred out of the sprint on 2026-10-19 (Glenn: not for the rocketnet v1.0.0 release; moved to the roadmap) with nova-sprint defer; not started in the sprint. :brief-file holds the card's whole brief as defer wrote it." :task "THE RULE. docs/SPEC-TABLES.md §2.13.1 \"Unbounded text: `[]string` and `map[string]V`\": an element or key with no length bound rides as kind 12 exactly as a bounded one, is never clamped and never dropped for its length, and compares by §2.8's order at any length. Oracle: internal/codegen/gotable/unboundedtext_test.go TestGoTableUnboundedTextListsAndMapKeys." :brief-file "docs/roadmap-briefs/schema-cards-out-2026-10-19.sexp")
  (:id "sprint-out/js-cook-carries-the-wide-kinds" :type :task :title "JavaScript's cooked form reads and writes the wide kinds: 128-bit integers and fixed point" :state :todo :evidence nil :sprint-card "js-cook-carries-the-wide-kinds" :sprint-column "waiting" :sprint-stream "schema-js" :sprint-base "sprint/schema-js" :tier "pro" :needs "js-base-forward-merge-schema-go" :pushed-head "" :pushed-branch "" :note "Waiting card js-cook-carries-the-wide-kinds of stream schema-js, deferred out of the sprint on 2026-10-19 (Glenn: not for the rocketnet v1.0.0 release; moved to the roadmap) with nova-sprint defer; not started in the sprint. :brief-file holds the card's whole brief as defer wrote it." :task "THE RULE. docs/SPEC-TABLES.md §7 and §7.6 (Cook and CookMeasure; cook writers can be any language) with §15's wide kinds: Go's cook reader and writer carry `int128`/`uint128` and `fixed(I, F)` nodes. Oracle: internal/codegen/gotable/cook.go and cookwrite.go at d808c3f54." :brief-file "docs/roadmap-briefs/schema-cards-out-2026-10-19.sexp")
  (:id "sprint-out/js-enum-variant-deprecated-in-place" :type :task :title "JavaScript: a deprecated enum variant reads as the field default and is refused on write" :state :todo :evidence nil :sprint-card "js-enum-variant-deprecated-in-place" :sprint-column "waiting" :sprint-stream "schema-js" :sprint-base "sprint/schema-js" :tier "pro" :needs "schema-go-enum-variant-deprecated-codegen,js-base-forward-merge-schema-go" :pushed-head "" :pushed-branch "" :note "Waiting card js-enum-variant-deprecated-in-place of stream schema-js, deferred out of the sprint on 2026-10-19 (Glenn: not for the rocketnet v1.0.0 release; moved to the roadmap) with nova-sprint defer; not started in the sprint. :brief-file holds the card's whole brief as defer wrote it." :task "RULING (Glenn, 2026-10-18): \"If it's possible to implement, then implement it!\" Enum variants may be deprecated in place (`| deprecated`), one way only. The standard (docs/SPEC-TABLES.md, card spec-enum-variant-deprecated-in-place) and the Go reference (cards schema-go-enum-variant-deprecated-front-end and schema-go-enum-variant-deprecated-codegen) define it; this port matches Go." :brief-file "docs/roadmap-briefs/schema-cards-out-2026-10-19.sexp")
  (:id "sprint-out/js-fixed-count-and-length-over-bound-refuse-by-name" :type :task :title "JavaScript: a fixed-form count or text length past its bound refuses by name" :state :todo :evidence nil :sprint-card "js-fixed-count-and-length-over-bound-refuse-by-name" :sprint-column "waiting" :sprint-stream "schema-js" :sprint-base "sprint/schema-js" :tier "pro" :needs "js-base-forward-merge-schema-go" :pushed-head "" :pushed-branch "" :note "Waiting card js-fixed-count-and-length-over-bound-refuse-by-name of stream schema-js, deferred out of the sprint on 2026-10-19 (Glenn: not for the rocketnet v1.0.0 release; moved to the roadmap) with nova-sprint defer; not started in the sprint. :brief-file holds the card's whole brief as defer wrote it." :task "THE RULE. docs/SPEC-TABLES.md §3.4 (THE RECORD; the plan's `count` and `text` ops) and docs/FIXED-FORM-ALGORITHM.md §4.5, commit 4edb98c8a: a count past the PLAN's bound refuses `count_over_bound` and a text length past the plan's cap refuses `length_over_bound`, both checked before any destination byte is written so REFUSE stays total. The ranged-scalar clamp (§4.6) is unchanged. Oracle: internal/codegen/gotable/fixedbound_test.go TestFixedFormCountAndLengthOverBoundRefuseByName (identity and compiled lineage plans)." :brief-file "docs/roadmap-briefs/schema-cards-out-2026-10-19.sexp")
  (:id "sprint-out/js-fixed-load-names-every-refusal" :type :task :title "JavaScript: every FixedLoad refusal carries its name, framing damage included" :state :todo :evidence nil :sprint-card "js-fixed-load-names-every-refusal" :sprint-column "waiting" :sprint-stream "schema-js" :sprint-base "sprint/schema-js" :tier "pro" :needs "js-base-forward-merge-schema-go" :pushed-head "" :pushed-branch "" :note "Waiting card js-fixed-load-names-every-refusal of stream schema-js, deferred out of the sprint on 2026-10-19 (Glenn: not for the rocketnet v1.0.0 release; moved to the roadmap) with nova-sprint defer; not started in the sprint. :brief-file holds the card's whole brief as defer wrote it." :task "THE RULE. docs/FIXED-FORM-ALGORITHM.md §5.3 and docs/SPEC-TABLES.md §11 (refused by name), §21.3: every refusal of `<Name>FixedLoad` has a name equal to one of the exported reason spellings, and the framing-damage returns keep `malformed` set beside the name. Go's set at d808c3f54 (internal/codegen/gotable/fixedruntime.go TableFixedReason*): previous_form, message_form_as_file, newer_form, layout_malformed, layout_unknown, layout_newer (reserved: no load answers it), layout_unsupported, layout_record_too_large, plan_too_large, batch_too_large, no_layout, text_ill_formed, truncated, reserved_not_zero, count_over_bound, length_over_bound. Oracle: internal/codegen/gotable/fixedrefusalnames_test.go TestFixedLoadNamesEveryRefusal." :brief-file "docs/roadmap-briefs/schema-cards-out-2026-10-19.sexp")
  (:id "sprint-out/js-plain-fixed-load-is-strict" :type :task :title "JavaScript: the plain FixedLoad is strict; FixedLoadTolerant keeps today's answers" :state :todo :evidence nil :sprint-card "js-plain-fixed-load-is-strict" :sprint-column "waiting" :sprint-stream "schema-js" :sprint-base "sprint/schema-js" :tier "pro" :needs "js-base-forward-merge-schema-go" :pushed-head "" :pushed-branch "" :note "Waiting card js-plain-fixed-load-is-strict of stream schema-js, deferred out of the sprint on 2026-10-19 (Glenn: not for the rocketnet v1.0.0 release; moved to the roadmap) with nova-sprint defer; not started in the sprint. :brief-file holds the card's whole brief as defer wrote it." :task "THE RULE. docs/SPEC-TABLES.md §6.5 (THE PLAIN NAME IS THE STRICT READ): the plain `<Name>FixedLoad` refuses (answers -1) whatever the strict read refuses, resets every value it had written, and the reason reaches the caller through the report; `<Name>FixedLoadTolerant` keeps the signature and the answers the plain name had. Per §3.3's float table a fixed read of a NaN or infinity is NOT a refusal. Oracle: TestGoDefaultReadIsStrict's \"fixed\" subtest (internal/codegen/gotable/strictdefault_test.go)." :brief-file "docs/roadmap-briefs/schema-cards-out-2026-10-19.sexp")
  (:id "sprint-out/js-plain-float-special-values-take-one-rule" :type :task :title "JavaScript: a plain float's -0 rides by bit pattern, and a NaN or infinity is named non_finite and refused by the strict read" :state :todo :evidence nil :sprint-card "js-plain-float-special-values-take-one-rule" :sprint-column "waiting" :sprint-stream "schema-js" :sprint-base "sprint/schema-js" :tier "pro" :needs "js-base-forward-merge-schema-go,js-plain-variable-load-is-strict,js-plain-load-messages-is-strict" :pushed-head "" :pushed-branch "" :note "Waiting card js-plain-float-special-values-take-one-rule of stream schema-js, deferred out of the sprint on 2026-10-19 (Glenn: not for the rocketnet v1.0.0 release; moved to the roadmap) with nova-sprint defer; not started in the sprint. :brief-file holds the card's whole brief as defer wrote it." :task "THE RULE. docs/SPEC-TABLES.md §3.3 \"A PLAIN FLOAT'S SPECIAL VALUES TAKE ONE RULE, IN EVERY FORM\" (and its table): default ELISION COMPARES BIT PATTERNS, so a -0 under a +0 default rides (and +0 under a declared -0 default), at every elision (a scalar field, a [N] array left off, an enum-keyed slot) in the variable and the message forms; a NaN or an infinity rides the binary forms bit for bit, the tolerant read lands it and counts nothing but NAMES the field in the report's reason as `non_finite: <Table>.<field>` (first name wins), and the strict read refuses it with `non_finite`. The fixed form carries it whole and names nothing. Oracle: internal/codegen/gotable/floatspecial_test.go TestGoPlainFloatSpecialValuesAgreeAcrossForms (four schemas: fs, fsFlat, fsKeyed, fsNeg)." :brief-file "docs/roadmap-briefs/schema-cards-out-2026-10-19.sexp")
  (:id "sprint-out/js-plain-load-messages-is-strict" :type :task :title "JavaScript: the plain LoadMessages is strict; LoadMessagesTolerant keeps today's answers" :state :todo :evidence nil :sprint-card "js-plain-load-messages-is-strict" :sprint-column "waiting" :sprint-stream "schema-js" :sprint-base "sprint/schema-js" :tier "pro" :needs "js-base-forward-merge-schema-go" :pushed-head "" :pushed-branch "" :note "Waiting card js-plain-load-messages-is-strict of stream schema-js, deferred out of the sprint on 2026-10-19 (Glenn: not for the rocketnet v1.0.0 release; moved to the roadmap) with nova-sprint defer; not started in the sprint. :brief-file holds the card's whole brief as defer wrote it." :task "THE RULE. docs/SPEC-TABLES.md §6.5: the message read `<Name>LoadMessages` is a plain name and refuses whatever the strict read refuses, answering ok == false; its count is 0 when the strict rule alone refused (every value it had written reset) and what the tolerant read answered when the tolerant read itself stopped on a body (the records ahead of it keep what they decoded). `<Name>LoadMessagesTolerant` keeps today's signature and answers. Oracle: TestGoDefaultReadIsStrict (the fixed root's LoadMessages leg) and internal/codegen/gotable/message*.go at d808c3f54." :brief-file "docs/roadmap-briefs/schema-cards-out-2026-10-19.sexp")
  (:id "sprint-out/js-plain-variable-load-is-strict" :type :task :title "JavaScript: the plain variable read is the strict read; the tolerant read has its own name" :state :todo :evidence nil :sprint-card "js-plain-variable-load-is-strict" :sprint-column "waiting" :sprint-stream "schema-js" :sprint-base "sprint/schema-js" :tier "pro" :needs "js-base-forward-merge-schema-go" :pushed-head "" :pushed-branch "" :note "Waiting card js-plain-variable-load-is-strict of stream schema-js, deferred out of the sprint on 2026-10-19 (Glenn: not for the rocketnet v1.0.0 release; moved to the roadmap) with nova-sprint defer; not started in the sprint. :brief-file holds the card's whole brief as defer wrote it." :task "THE RULE. docs/SPEC-TABLES.md §6.5 (\"THE PLAIN NAME IS THE STRICT READ; THE TOLERANT READ HAS A NAME OF ITS OWN\", and \"The STRICT read\") and §11: every generated read entry point a caller reaches by the plain name refuses whatever the strict read refuses (malformed, clamped, kind_mismatch, an unknown form, wire damage, build-version mismatch, missing_required) and hands back no recovered value; the tolerant read keeps the recovered value and its report under an explicit `...Tolerant` name; `<Name>ReadStrict(wire)` answers the root or refuses with one typed reason; `unknown`, `widened` and `retained` alone never refuse. Oracle: internal/codegen/gotable/strictdefault_test.go TestGoDefaultReadIsStrict and commits 61105d0b1, 1f53ff49d, f995112ac, bcff9c99e, 2c0700baa." :brief-file "docs/roadmap-briefs/schema-cards-out-2026-10-19.sexp")
  (:id "sprint-out/js-savetext-loadtext-carry-canonical-base64" :type :task :title "JavaScript: every table carries SaveText and LoadText, canonical base64 over the binary wire" :state :todo :evidence nil :sprint-card "js-savetext-loadtext-carry-canonical-base64" :sprint-column "waiting" :sprint-stream "schema-js" :sprint-base "sprint/schema-js" :tier "pro" :needs "js-base-forward-merge-schema-go" :pushed-head "" :pushed-branch "" :note "Waiting card js-savetext-loadtext-carry-canonical-base64 of stream schema-js, deferred out of the sprint on 2026-10-19 (Glenn: not for the rocketnet v1.0.0 release; moved to the roadmap) with nova-sprint defer; not started in the sprint. :brief-file holds the card's whole brief as defer wrote it." :task "THE RULE. docs/SPEC-TABLES.md §16.8: EVERY TABLE HAS BOTH text carriers. `<Name>SaveText` writes the wire `<Name>Save` writes as CANONICAL base64 (standard alphabet, padded, pad bits zero, no whitespace); `<Name>LoadText(text, report)` IS THE STRICT READ for both classes: a text whose CR/LF-stripped form decodes but is not exactly canonical is `base64_not_canonical`, every other failure `base64_damaged`, a decoded wire the binary reader refuses keeps that reader's own refusal, and a read whose report holds an error refuses whatever the tolerant load answered. Both suffixes are in §11's claimed list. Oracle: internal/codegen/gotable/base64canonical_test.go TestGoLoadTextRefusesNonCanonicalBase64 (the fuzz repro `AQAAAAAAAAAAAB==`). The JSON half (bytes fields inside a JSON text) is schema-go-json-base64-canonical, still WORKING on schema-go: not this card." :brief-file "docs/roadmap-briefs/schema-cards-out-2026-10-19.sexp")
  (:id "sprint-out/js-testgen-writes-round-trip-and-damage-tests" :type :task :title "`schema testgen --lang js` writes each root table's round-trip and damage tests" :state :todo :evidence nil :sprint-card "js-testgen-writes-round-trip-and-damage-tests" :sprint-column "waiting" :sprint-stream "schema-js" :sprint-base "sprint/schema-js" :tier "pro" :needs "js-base-forward-merge-schema-go,js-savetext-loadtext-carry-canonical-base64" :pushed-head "" :pushed-branch "" :note "Waiting card js-testgen-writes-round-trip-and-damage-tests of stream schema-js, deferred out of the sprint on 2026-10-19 (Glenn: not for the rocketnet v1.0.0 release; moved to the roadmap) with nova-sprint defer; not started in the sprint. :brief-file holds the card's whole brief as defer wrote it." :task "THE RULE. docs/SPEC-TABLES.md §16.11 \"Generated round-trip and damage tests: `schema testgen`\": one test file per unit file declaring a root table, using the generated API and the language's standard library only, a value through the binary, base64 and JSON carriers and back, and a damaged input refused by name; a table whose forms leave out wire or json is refused by name. Oracle: internal/codegen/gotable/testgen.go and its tests." :brief-file "docs/roadmap-briefs/schema-cards-out-2026-10-19.sexp")
  (:id "sprint-out/js-text-zero-byte-refuses-the-read" :type :task :title "JavaScript: a JSON string that decodes to U+0000 in text storage refuses the read as text_holds_zero" :state :todo :evidence nil :sprint-card "js-text-zero-byte-refuses-the-read" :sprint-column "waiting" :sprint-stream "schema-js" :sprint-base "sprint/schema-js" :tier "pro" :needs "js-base-forward-merge-schema-go,js-plain-variable-load-is-strict" :pushed-head "" :pushed-branch "" :note "Waiting card js-text-zero-byte-refuses-the-read of stream schema-js, deferred out of the sprint on 2026-10-19 (Glenn: not for the rocketnet v1.0.0 release; moved to the roadmap) with nova-sprint defer; not started in the sprint. :brief-file holds the card's whole brief as defer wrote it." :task "THE RULE. docs/SPEC-TABLES.md §16.3 \"A ZERO IN TEXT TAKES ONE RULE IN EVERY FORM: NO READ STORES IT\": a JSON string the read would PLACE in text storage (a string(N), *string, wstring(N) value, a text-list element, a map key) that decodes to U+0000 refuses the read: FromJson returns false (null here), the report is malformed (one event, one malformed) and the reason reads `text_holds_zero: <Table>.<field>` for the innermost field; a string the read only SKIPS (an unknown key's value) is not the event; a \\u0001 reads clean. Oracle: internal/codegen/gotable/textzero_test.go TestGoTextZeroByteTakesOneRuleInEveryForm." :brief-file "docs/roadmap-briefs/schema-cards-out-2026-10-19.sexp")
  (:id "sprint-out/js-timestamp-text-is-strict-rfc3339" :type :task :title "JavaScript's timestamp text is strict RFC 3339 §5.6 date-time, read and written as Go does" :state :todo :evidence nil :sprint-card "js-timestamp-text-is-strict-rfc3339" :sprint-column "waiting" :sprint-stream "schema-js" :sprint-base "sprint/schema-js" :tier "pro" :needs "js-base-forward-merge-schema-go,js-carries-timestamp-on-the-table-wires" :pushed-head "" :pushed-branch "" :note "Waiting card js-timestamp-text-is-strict-rfc3339 of stream schema-js, deferred out of the sprint on 2026-10-19 (Glenn: not for the rocketnet v1.0.0 release; moved to the roadmap) with nova-sprint defer; not started in the sprint. :brief-file holds the card's whole brief as defer wrote it." :task "THE RULE. docs/SPEC-TABLES.md §2.11 and §16.2, commit 7fb89e941: a timestamp's JSON text is a strict RFC 3339 section 5.6 date-time; anything else refuses the read as `timestamp_not_rfc3339`; the writer writes Go's canonical spelling. Oracles: internal/rfc3339 TestStrictRFC3339, internal/codegen/gotable/timestampstrict_test.go TestGoTimestampStrictRFC3339, TestTextFormTimestampStrictRFC3339." :brief-file "docs/roadmap-briefs/schema-cards-out-2026-10-19.sexp")
  (:id "sprint-out/js-view-carries-exact-ranges-and-unbounded-container" :type :task :title "JavaScript: the field descriptor carries the exact integer range, the wide raw range and UnboundedContainer" :state :todo :evidence nil :sprint-card "js-view-carries-exact-ranges-and-unbounded-container" :sprint-column "waiting" :sprint-stream "schema-js" :sprint-base "sprint/schema-js" :tier "pro" :needs "js-base-forward-merge-schema-go" :pushed-head "" :pushed-branch "" :note "Waiting card js-view-carries-exact-ranges-and-unbounded-container of stream schema-js, deferred out of the sprint on 2026-10-19 (Glenn: not for the rocketnet v1.0.0 release; moved to the roadmap) with nova-sprint defer; not started in the sprint. :brief-file holds the card's whole brief as defer wrote it." :task "THE RULE. docs/SPEC-TABLES.md §8.1: a ranged integer field carries its EXACT range beside the double pair (int64 columns for signed, uint64 for unsigned and bits(N), the implied range for bits(N)), a wide-kind field carries its frac bits and its exact raw range, and a map or an unbounded array carries `UnboundedContainer` true with array_bound 0 (the ONE TELL that tells \"no bound\" from a bound of 2^31 - 1), §2.9. Oracles: internal/codegen/gotable/exactrange_test.go TestGoExactIntegerRangeBounds (the descriptor half: RangeIntMax 9007199254740993 exact, an int128 carrying no int64 pair) and internal/codegen/gotable/unboundeddescriptor_test.go TestGoUnboundedDescriptorIsExplicit (the descriptor half)." :brief-file "docs/roadmap-briefs/schema-cards-out-2026-10-19.sexp")
  (:id "sprint-out/rust-base-forward-merge-schema-go" :type :task :title "sprint/schema-rust takes sprint/schema-go: the Rust base forward-merge" :state :todo :evidence nil :sprint-card "rust-base-forward-merge-schema-go" :sprint-column "review" :sprint-stream "schema-rust" :sprint-base "sprint/schema-rust" :tier "heavy" :needs "none" :pushed-head "53ef1b3c5aebce7740cba374516fbf8bded674b9" :pushed-branch "sprint/rust-base-forward-merge-schema-go.w6.g1.e21" :note "Carried: branch sprint/rust-base-forward-merge-schema-go.w6.g1.e21 head 53ef1b3c5aebce7740cba374516fbf8bded674b9 (attempt 9, review). Task: sprint/schema-rust takes sprint/schema-go: the Rust base forward-merge. Moved out of the sprint on 2026-10-19 (Glenn: \"Please take all work in the current sprint that is not for this rocketnet release and push it out to the appropriate roadmap sexp\"): sprint card rust-base-forward-merge-schema-go of stream schema-rust was in review, not landed; the card was dropped from the sprint naming this item, and its pushed head stays on that branch. :brief-file holds the card's whole brief at the move." :task "THE TASK. sprint/schema-rust is about 730 commits behind sprint/schema-go (64dc1ddd when carded; GO TIP below is the tip you fetch, at or after it). Merge origin/sprint/schema-go into the base as ONE merge commit on the card branch: git fetch origin, then git merge --no-ff GO TIP. Never a rebase, never a squash, never a force-push. A trial merge on 2026-10-18 left these conflicts (a newer GO TIP may add a few; resolve those by the same rules): .github/workflows/cla.yml, ROADMAP.md, bench/BENCH-STANDARD.md, compiler/tableslists_test.go, docs/SPEC-TABLES.md, generated/bench/paired/go/BenchTableJson.go, generated/bench/paired/rust/lib.rs, generated/bench/paired/rust/message_runtime.rs, generated/bench/tables/go/BenchTableTableJson.go, internal/check/check.go, internal/check/tables_test.go, internal/codegen/ctable/fixedform.go, internal/codegen/gotable/json.go, internal/codegen/rusttable/fixedform.go, internal/tablenames/js.go, make/negative-controls.json. Resolve each conflict keeping BOTH sides' intent, by these rules and no others: shared Go and IR code (ir/, internal/check/, internal/parser/, compiler/, internal/codegen/gotable/, tools/, .github/) takes GO TIP's version; port-speci [...]" :brief-file "docs/roadmap-briefs/schema-cards-out-2026-10-19.sexp")
