  (:id "sprint-out/schema-java-emitter-nullness-annotations" :type :task :title "The Java emitter writes the null-sentinel pattern without nullness annotations: NullAway reports 19,789 findings on the generated corpus" :state :todo :evidence nil :sprint-card "schema-java-emitter-nullness-annotations" :sprint-column "review" :sprint-stream "schema-java" :sprint-base "sprint/schema-java" :tier "heavy" :needs "" :pushed-head "07567e3b5f1ea9c1b7b891d1f89ff2dafb09886d" :pushed-branch "sprint/schema-java-emitter-nullness-annotations.w2.g2.e21" :note "Carried: branch sprint/schema-java-emitter-nullness-annotations.w2.g2.e21 head 07567e3b5f1ea9c1b7b891d1f89ff2dafb09886d (attempt 4, review). Task: The Java emitter writes the null-sentinel pattern without nullness annotations: NullAway reports 19,789 findings on the generated corpus. Moved out of the sprint on 2026-10-19 (Glenn: \"Please take all work in the current sprint that is not for this rocketnet release and push it out to the appropriate roadmap sexp\"): sprint card schema-java-emitter-nullness-annotations of stream schema-java was in review, not landed; the card was dropped from the sprint naming this item, and its pushed head stays on that branch. :brief-file holds the card's whole brief at the move." :task "RULING (coordinator, 2026-10-19, on j29257): the NullAway corpus gate (schema-java-generated-errorprone-nullaway-gate) is red on 19,789 findings, all from the null-sentinel pattern in generated Java. We do NOT blanket-suppress them. The javatable emitter emits nullness annotations instead. The gate card waits on this one: it cannot pass without the annotations." :brief-file "docs/roadmap-briefs/schema-cards-out-2026-10-19.sexp")
  (:id "sprint-out/schema-java-fixed-tables-are-private-and-immutable" :type :task :title "Java generated fixed tables: private and immutable to callers" :state :todo :evidence nil :sprint-card "schema-java-fixed-tables-are-private-and-immutable" :sprint-column "review" :sprint-stream "schema-java" :sprint-base "sprint/schema-java" :tier "pro" :needs "" :pushed-head "f7328d5b38aa74cb0d9172b6d28bd89ab91dc036" :pushed-branch "sprint/schema-java-fixed-tables-are-private-and-immutable.w4.g1.e21" :note "Carried: branch sprint/schema-java-fixed-tables-are-private-and-immutable.w4.g1.e21 head f7328d5b38aa74cb0d9172b6d28bd89ab91dc036 (attempt 4, review). Task: Java generated fixed tables: private and immutable to callers. Moved out of the sprint on 2026-10-19 (Glenn: \"Please take all work in the current sprint that is not for this rocketnet release and push it out to the appropriate roadmap sexp\"): sprint card schema-java-fixed-tables-are-private-and-immutable of stream schema-java was in review, not landed; the card was dropped from the sprint naming this item, and its pushed head stays on that branch. :brief-file holds the card's whole brief at the move." :task "WHY. The Java SpotBugs lens (card schema-java-generated-spotbugs-gate, triage list triage-findings-medium-unfiltered.xml in its receipts) found 512 real MS_PKGPROTECT findings: generated fixed-table classes expose public static arrays (layout, defaults, dest, known and the like) whose elements any caller can overwrite, corrupting the decode tables for the whole process. Test code in other packages reads these arrays today. Hot read path stays zero-allocation: the generated code reads its own private table directly; only outside callers go through an accessor." :brief-file "docs/roadmap-briefs/schema-cards-out-2026-10-19.sexp")
  (:id "sprint-out/schema-java-generated-checker-signedness" :type :task :title "Java Checker Framework signedness checker (java port of schema)" :state :todo :evidence nil :sprint-card "schema-java-generated-checker-signedness" :sprint-column "ready" :sprint-stream "schema-java" :sprint-base "sprint/schema-java" :tier "pro" :needs "" :pushed-head "497cf90c8c46310e5685d611fe17b88f5a24570e" :pushed-branch "sprint/schema-java-generated-checker-signedness.w3.g3.e21" :note "Carried: branch sprint/schema-java-generated-checker-signedness.w3.g3.e21 head 497cf90c8c46310e5685d611fe17b88f5a24570e (attempt 9, ready). Task: Java Checker Framework signedness checker (java port of schema). Moved out of the sprint on 2026-10-19 (Glenn: \"Please take all work in the current sprint that is not for this rocketnet release and push it out to the appropriate roadmap sexp\"): sprint card schema-java-generated-checker-signedness of stream schema-java was in ready, not landed; the card was dropped from the sprint naming this item, and its pushed head stays on that branch. :brief-file holds the card's whole brief at the move." :task "THE LENS. Schema generates the same algorithm in many languages, so every language's strictest checker, run over the generated output for the schema repository's test-schema corpus (every schema under the corpus directories the Makefile's generate targets read, found with grep -n in the Makefile and make/*.mk; do not invent a second corpus), is a separate lens on bugs (Glenn, 2026-10-18; ideas roadmap group schema-per-language-lenses). THIS CARD: the Checker Framework signedness checker over the generated Java: unsigned bytes, shorts and ints held in signed Java types are a prime bug class, so annotate the generator output with @Unsigned/@Signed and let the checker prove every widening, comparison and shift over the generated java output (readers and writers, and the runtime where the port has one). Add PMD in the same target if it takes under an hour; otherwise say so and leave it for a later card." :brief-file "docs/roadmap-briefs/schema-cards-out-2026-10-19.sexp")
  (:id "sprint-out/schema-java-generated-errorprone-nullaway-gate" :type :task :title "Java Error Prone and NullAway gate (java port of schema)" :state :todo :evidence nil :sprint-card "schema-java-generated-errorprone-nullaway-gate" :sprint-column "waiting" :sprint-stream "schema-java" :sprint-base "sprint/schema-java" :tier "" :needs "schema-java-emitter-nullness-annotations" :pushed-head "" :pushed-branch "" :note "Waiting card schema-java-generated-errorprone-nullaway-gate of stream schema-java, deferred out of the sprint on 2026-10-19 (Glenn: not for the rocketnet v1.0.0 release; moved to the roadmap) with nova-sprint defer; not started in the sprint. :brief-file holds the card's whole brief as defer wrote it." :task "THE LENS. Schema generates the same algorithm in many languages, so every language's strictest checker, run over the generated output for the schema repository's test-schema corpus (every schema under the corpus directories the Makefile's generate targets read, found with grep -n in the Makefile and make/*.mk; do not invent a second corpus), is a separate lens on bugs (Glenn, 2026-10-18; ideas roadmap group schema-per-language-lenses). THIS CARD: Error Prone and NullAway as javac plugins over the generated Java (warnings as errors, justified suppressions only) over the generated java output (readers and writers, and the runtime where the port has one)." :brief-file "docs/roadmap-briefs/schema-cards-out-2026-10-19.sexp")
  (:id "sprint-out/schema-java-generated-spotbugs-gate" :type :task :title "Java SpotBugs gate (java port of schema)" :state :todo :evidence nil :sprint-card "schema-java-generated-spotbugs-gate" :sprint-column "waiting" :sprint-stream "schema-java" :sprint-base "sprint/schema-java" :tier "pro" :needs "" :pushed-head "8e9c6f31a4c5c449fbdb851543d3ca19db938d7a" :pushed-branch "" :note "Waiting card schema-java-generated-spotbugs-gate of stream schema-java, deferred out of the sprint on 2026-10-19 (Glenn: not for the rocketnet v1.0.0 release; moved to the roadmap) with nova-sprint defer; not started in the sprint. It carried an earlier head: schema-java-generated-spotbugs-gate attempt 1 head 8e9c6f31a4c5c449fbdb851543d3ca19db938d7a. :brief-file holds the card's whole brief as defer wrote it." :task "THE LENS. Schema generates the same algorithm in many languages, so every language's strictest checker, run over the generated output for the schema repository's test-schema corpus (every schema under the corpus directories the Makefile's generate targets read, found with grep -n in the Makefile and make/*.mk; do not invent a second corpus), is a separate lens on bugs (Glenn, 2026-10-18; ideas roadmap group schema-per-language-lenses). THIS CARD: SpotBugs (with the find-sec-bugs plugin) over the compiled generated Java, at the strictest effort/threshold that is not noise-dominated over the generated java output (readers and writers, and the runtime where the port has one)." :brief-file "docs/roadmap-briefs/schema-cards-out-2026-10-19.sexp")
  (:id "sprint-out/schema-java-nightly-fuzz" :type :task :title "nightly fuzzing (java port of schema)" :state :todo :evidence nil :sprint-card "schema-java-nightly-fuzz" :sprint-column "review" :sprint-stream "schema-java" :sprint-base "sprint/schema-java" :tier "pro" :needs "" :pushed-head "71687d278a2f8d11815fef63aaf43503ce15e2d2" :pushed-branch "sprint/schema-java-nightly-fuzz.w1.g1.e21" :note "Carried: branch sprint/schema-java-nightly-fuzz.w1.g1.e21 head 71687d278a2f8d11815fef63aaf43503ce15e2d2 (attempt 1, review). Task: nightly fuzzing (java port of schema). Moved out of the sprint on 2026-10-19 (Glenn: \"Please take all work in the current sprint that is not for this rocketnet release and push it out to the appropriate roadmap sexp\"): sprint card schema-java-nightly-fuzz of stream schema-java was in review, not landed; the card was dropped from the sprint naming this item, and its pushed head stays on that branch. :brief-file holds the card's whole brief at the move." :task "NIGHTLY FUZZING (Glenn, 2026-10-18). Fuzz the java port's generated readers with its native coverage-guided fuzzer: Jazzer. Targets: load, strict read and text/JSON parse for every table in a fuzz corpus schema set (pick the set from the schema repository's test-schema corpus (every schema under the corpus directories the Makefile's generate targets read, found with grep -n in the Makefile and make/*.mk; do not invent a second corpus) so that every table shape is covered, and list it in a file the harness reads). Seed the fuzzer from the Go fuzz corpus (internal/fuzz/testdata and the go test -fuzz seeds) and the conformance vectors. Use Jazzer fuzz targets (fuzzerTestOneInput) per reader kind." :brief-file "docs/roadmap-briefs/schema-cards-out-2026-10-19.sexp")
  (:id "sprint-out/schema-java-resource-bounds" :type :task :title "java port: bounded memory and time on hostile inputs (java port of schema)" :state :todo :evidence nil :sprint-card "schema-java-resource-bounds" :sprint-column "waiting" :sprint-stream "schema-java" :sprint-base "sprint/schema-java" :tier "pro" :needs "" :pushed-head "" :pushed-branch "" :note "Waiting card schema-java-resource-bounds of stream schema-java, deferred out of the sprint on 2026-10-19 (Glenn: not for the rocketnet v1.0.0 release; moved to the roadmap) with nova-sprint defer; not started in the sprint. :brief-file holds the card's whole brief as defer wrote it." :task "Denial-of-service hardening for the java port (Glenn, 2026-10-18). Using the bounds documented by schema-shared-resource-bounds-every-port (read it first), assert in this port that hostile inputs cost bounded memory and time: huge counts, deep nesting, recursion, giant strings and many unknown fields. Allocation is bounded by input size times the documented factor; nesting depth is capped and refused by name. Use a test with an allocation counter in this language (an allocator hook, a counting allocator, runtime memstats, GC counters or the nearest the language offers; name it). Time is asserted by operation count or step count, never by wall clock. A violation is a finding: red first, then fix in the generator or runtime; fix the port, and carry any cross-port gap as FIX-CARD: <slug>: <one line>." :brief-file "docs/roadmap-briefs/schema-cards-out-2026-10-19.sexp")
  (:id "sprint-out/schema-java-runs-hostile-corpus" :type :task :title "java port runs the whole hostile corpus in its unit tier (java port of schema)" :state :todo :evidence nil :sprint-card "schema-java-runs-hostile-corpus" :sprint-column "waiting" :sprint-stream "schema-java" :sprint-base "sprint/schema-java" :tier "pro" :needs "schema-shared-hostile-corpus,java-base-forward-merge-schema-go" :pushed-head "" :pushed-branch "" :note "Waiting card schema-java-runs-hostile-corpus of stream schema-java, deferred out of the sprint on 2026-10-19 (Glenn: not for the rocketnet v1.0.0 release; moved to the roadmap) with nova-sprint defer; not started in the sprint. :brief-file holds the card's whole brief as defer wrote it." :task "Make the java port run every input of the committed hostile corpus (built by schema-shared-hostile-corpus; read docs/HOSTILE-CORPUS.md and the manifest first) in its unit tier: for each input, the port's generated reader must reach the verdict the manifest holds (accept with the same decoded value digest, or refuse with the same named reason). The runner reads files only (no network, no real time). A mismatch is a finding: red first where it is a reader bug, carried as FIX-CARD: <slug>: <input> <one line>. Do not edit the corpus here; a wrong manifest verdict is reported against the engine card." :brief-file "docs/roadmap-briefs/schema-cards-out-2026-10-19.sexp")
  (:id "sprint-out/schema-js-checkjs-codec-literals-match-descriptor-type" :type :task :title "checkJs strict: codec and union literals do not match the shared descriptor type (~1,760 findings)" :state :todo :evidence nil :sprint-card "schema-js-checkjs-codec-literals-match-descriptor-type" :sprint-column "waiting" :sprint-stream "schema-js" :sprint-base "sprint/schema-js" :tier "heavy" :needs "schema-js-emitter-jsdoc-types" :pushed-head "" :pushed-branch "" :note "Waiting card schema-js-checkjs-codec-literals-match-descriptor-type of stream schema-js, deferred out of the sprint on 2026-10-19 (Glenn: not for the rocketnet v1.0.0 release; moved to the roadmap) with nova-sprint defer; not started in the sprint. :brief-file holds the card's whole brief as defer wrote it." :task "Source. The coordinator, 2026-10-19. Card schema-js-emitter-jsdoc-types (branch sprint/schema-js-emitter-jsdoc-types.w1.g1.e21, head 2b130c5e3) brought `tsc --checkJs --strict` over the generated JS corpus from 41,066 findings to 7,642 with JSDoc only; its report (NOT DONE 1) names the groups that remain, all needing real code changes. Card name of the whole: schema-js-checkjs-strict-to-zero, split into one card per group plus a last card that sets the gate's ratchet to 0. This card is one group. Real code changes in the JS emitter and the runtimes it emits are allowed. THE HARD RULE: the wire bytes stay byte-identical." :brief-file "docs/roadmap-briefs/schema-cards-out-2026-10-19.sexp")
