  (:id "sprint-out/schema-js-engine-differential" :type :task :title "JavaScript Node/Deno/browser-engine differential (js port of schema)" :state :todo :evidence nil :sprint-card "schema-js-engine-differential" :sprint-column "review" :sprint-stream "schema-js" :sprint-base "sprint/schema-js" :tier "pro" :needs "" :pushed-head "b1a0138b9d538aee75571f875fddb6437d702fc1" :pushed-branch "sprint/schema-js-engine-differential.w1.g1.e21" :note "Carried: branch sprint/schema-js-engine-differential.w1.g1.e21 head b1a0138b9d538aee75571f875fddb6437d702fc1 (attempt 1, review). Task: JavaScript Node/Deno/browser-engine differential (js port of schema). Moved out of the sprint on 2026-10-19 (Glenn: \"Please take all work in the current sprint that is not for this rocketnet release and push it out to the appropriate roadmap sexp\"): sprint card schema-js-engine-differential of stream schema-js was in review, not landed; the card was dropped from the sprint naming this item, and its pushed head stays on that branch. :brief-file holds the card's whole brief at the move." :task "THE LENS. Schema generates the same algorithm in many languages, so every language's strictest checker, run over the generated output for the schema repository's test-schema corpus (every schema under the corpus directories the Makefile's generate targets read, found with grep -n in the Makefile and make/*.mk; do not invent a second corpus), is a separate lens on bugs (Glenn, 2026-10-18; ideas roadmap group schema-per-language-lenses). THIS CARD: a differential run of the generated JS conformance tests on Node, Deno and a headless browser engine, checking BigInt and number semantics agree and that every port-level result is identical over the generated js output (readers and writers, and the runtime where the port has one). Heavy: nightly only." :brief-file "docs/roadmap-briefs/schema-cards-out-2026-10-19.sexp")
