  (:id "sprint-out/schema-js-resource-bounds" :type :task :title "js port: bounded memory and time on hostile inputs (js port of schema)" :state :todo :evidence nil :sprint-card "schema-js-resource-bounds" :sprint-column "waiting" :sprint-stream "schema-js" :sprint-base "sprint/schema-js" :tier "pro" :needs "" :pushed-head "" :pushed-branch "" :note "Waiting card schema-js-resource-bounds of stream schema-js, deferred out of the sprint on 2026-10-19 (Glenn: not for the rocketnet v1.0.0 release; moved to the roadmap) with nova-sprint defer; not started in the sprint. :brief-file holds the card's whole brief as defer wrote it." :task "Denial-of-service hardening for the js port (Glenn, 2026-10-18). Using the bounds documented by schema-shared-resource-bounds-every-port (read it first), assert in this port that hostile inputs cost bounded memory and time: huge counts, deep nesting, recursion, giant strings and many unknown fields. Allocation is bounded by input size times the documented factor; nesting depth is capped and refused by name. Use a test with an allocation counter in this language (an allocator hook, a counting allocator, runtime memstats, GC counters or the nearest the language offers; name it). Time is asserted by operation count or step count, never by wall clock. A violation is a finding: red first, then fix in the generator or runtime; fix the port, and carry any cross-port gap as FIX-CARD: <slug>: <one line>." :brief-file "docs/roadmap-briefs/schema-cards-out-2026-10-19.sexp")
  (:id "sprint-out/schema-js-runs-hostile-corpus" :type :task :title "js port runs the whole hostile corpus in its unit tier (js port of schema)" :state :todo :evidence nil :sprint-card "schema-js-runs-hostile-corpus" :sprint-column "waiting" :sprint-stream "schema-js" :sprint-base "sprint/schema-js" :tier "pro" :needs "" :pushed-head "" :pushed-branch "" :note "Waiting card schema-js-runs-hostile-corpus of stream schema-js, deferred out of the sprint on 2026-10-19 (Glenn: not for the rocketnet v1.0.0 release; moved to the roadmap) with nova-sprint defer; not started in the sprint. :brief-file holds the card's whole brief as defer wrote it." :task "Make the js port run every input of the committed hostile corpus (built by schema-shared-hostile-corpus; read docs/HOSTILE-CORPUS.md and the manifest first) in its unit tier: for each input, the port's generated reader must reach the verdict the manifest holds (accept with the same decoded value digest, or refuse with the same named reason). The runner reads files only (no network, no real time). A mismatch is a finding: red first where it is a reader bug, carried as FIX-CARD: <slug>: <input> <one line>. Do not edit the corpus here; a wrong manifest verdict is reported against the engine card." :brief-file "docs/roadmap-briefs/schema-cards-out-2026-10-19.sexp")
  (:id "sprint-out/schema-rust-generated-clippy-miri-gate" :type :task :title "Rust clippy and Miri gate (rust port of schema)" :state :todo :evidence nil :sprint-card "schema-rust-generated-clippy-miri-gate" :sprint-column "review" :sprint-stream "schema-rust" :sprint-base "sprint/schema-rust" :tier "pro" :needs "" :pushed-head "ef944c4f2f048b9f8c0b47ae7c198c4918ef636a" :pushed-branch "sprint/schema-rust-generated-clippy-miri-gate.w2.g1.e21" :note "Carried: branch sprint/schema-rust-generated-clippy-miri-gate.w2.g1.e21 head ef944c4f2f048b9f8c0b47ae7c198c4918ef636a (attempt 2, review). Task: Rust clippy and Miri gate (rust port of schema). Moved out of the sprint on 2026-10-19 (Glenn: \"Please take all work in the current sprint that is not for this rocketnet release and push it out to the appropriate roadmap sexp\"): sprint card schema-rust-generated-clippy-miri-gate of stream schema-rust was in review, not landed; the card was dropped from the sprint naming this item, and its pushed head stays on that branch. :brief-file holds the card's whole brief at the move." :task "THE LENS. Schema generates the same algorithm in many languages, so every language's strictest checker, run over the generated output for the schema repository's test-schema corpus (every schema under the corpus directories the Makefile's generate targets read, found with grep -n in the Makefile and make/*.mk; do not invent a second corpus), is a separate lens on bugs (Glenn, 2026-10-18; ideas roadmap group schema-per-language-lenses). THIS CARD: clippy -D warnings (pedantic, with justified allows) over the runtime and generated units, and Miri over the runtime and generated units tests (undefined behaviour); also forbid(unsafe_code) where the unit needs no unsafe, and overflow-checks = true in release over the generated rust output (readers and writers, and the runtime where the port has one). Miri is slow: nightly, with the smallest test set that still covers every reader kind." :brief-file "docs/roadmap-briefs/schema-cards-out-2026-10-19.sexp")
  (:id "sprint-out/schema-rust-generated-kani-readers" :type :task :title "Rust Kani on the generated readers (rust port of schema)" :state :todo :evidence nil :sprint-card "schema-rust-generated-kani-readers" :sprint-column "review" :sprint-stream "schema-rust" :sprint-base "sprint/schema-rust" :tier "pro" :needs "" :pushed-head "4e2e860feafd6cf0df1edd2c1cb8df39281c85e0" :pushed-branch "sprint/schema-rust-generated-kani-readers.w1.g3.e21" :note "Carried: branch sprint/schema-rust-generated-kani-readers.w1.g3.e21 head 4e2e860feafd6cf0df1edd2c1cb8df39281c85e0 (attempt 1, review). Task: Rust Kani on the generated readers (rust port of schema). Moved out of the sprint on 2026-10-19 (Glenn: \"Please take all work in the current sprint that is not for this rocketnet release and push it out to the appropriate roadmap sexp\"): sprint card schema-rust-generated-kani-readers of stream schema-rust was in review, not landed; the card was dropped from the sprint naming this item, and its pushed head stays on that branch. :brief-file holds the card's whole brief at the move." :task "THE LENS. Schema generates the same algorithm in many languages, so every language's strictest checker, run over the generated output for the schema repository's test-schema corpus (every schema under the corpus directories the Makefile's generate targets read, found with grep -n in the Makefile and make/*.mk; do not invent a second corpus), is a separate lens on bugs (Glenn, 2026-10-18; ideas roadmap group schema-per-language-lenses). THIS CARD: Kani model checking of the generated Rust readers (no panic, no overflow, no out-of-bounds for any input up to a stated bound) over the generated rust output (readers and writers, and the runtime where the port has one). Heavy: nightly only." :brief-file "docs/roadmap-briefs/schema-cards-out-2026-10-19.sexp")
  (:id "sprint-out/schema-rust-nightly-fuzz" :type :task :title "nightly fuzzing (rust port of schema)" :state :todo :evidence nil :sprint-card "schema-rust-nightly-fuzz" :sprint-column "waiting" :sprint-stream "schema-rust" :sprint-base "sprint/schema-rust" :tier "pro" :needs "" :pushed-head "95977dfb7ec7b6d548ed9d137afaa97326682d79" :pushed-branch "" :note "Waiting card schema-rust-nightly-fuzz of stream schema-rust, deferred out of the sprint on 2026-10-19 (Glenn: not for the rocketnet v1.0.0 release; moved to the roadmap) with nova-sprint defer; not started in the sprint. It carried an earlier head: schema-rust-nightly-fuzz attempt 8 head 95977dfb7ec7b6d548ed9d137afaa97326682d79. :brief-file holds the card's whole brief as defer wrote it." :task "NIGHTLY FUZZING (Glenn, 2026-10-18). Fuzz the rust port's generated readers with its native coverage-guided fuzzer: cargo-fuzz (libFuzzer). Targets: load, strict read and text/JSON parse for every table in a fuzz corpus schema set (pick the set from the schema repository's test-schema corpus (every schema under the corpus directories the Makefile's generate targets read, found with grep -n in the Makefile and make/*.mk; do not invent a second corpus) so that every table shape is covered, and list it in a file the harness reads). Seed the fuzzer from the Go fuzz corpus (internal/fuzz/testdata and the go test -fuzz seeds) and the conformance vectors. Use cargo +nightly fuzz with one fuzz_target per reader kind." :brief-file "docs/roadmap-briefs/schema-cards-out-2026-10-19.sexp")
