  (:id "sprint-out/schema-rust-runs-hostile-corpus" :type :task :title "rust port runs the whole hostile corpus in its unit tier (rust port of schema)" :state :todo :evidence nil :sprint-card "schema-rust-runs-hostile-corpus" :sprint-column "review" :sprint-stream "schema-rust" :sprint-base "sprint/schema-rust" :tier "pro" :needs "" :pushed-head "134c23377063a292ae5cd53c5d6132af7da3fc2b" :pushed-branch "sprint/schema-rust-runs-hostile-corpus.w2.g2.e21" :note "Carried: branch sprint/schema-rust-runs-hostile-corpus.w2.g2.e21 head 134c23377063a292ae5cd53c5d6132af7da3fc2b (attempt 6, review). Task: rust port runs the whole hostile corpus in its unit tier (rust port of schema). Moved out of the sprint on 2026-10-19 (Glenn: \"Please take all work in the current sprint that is not for this rocketnet release and push it out to the appropriate roadmap sexp\"): sprint card schema-rust-runs-hostile-corpus of stream schema-rust was in review, not landed; the card was dropped from the sprint naming this item, and its pushed head stays on that branch. :brief-file holds the card's whole brief at the move." :task "Make the rust port run every input of the committed hostile corpus (built by schema-shared-hostile-corpus; read docs/HOSTILE-CORPUS.md and the manifest first) in its unit tier: for each input, the port's generated reader must reach the verdict the manifest holds (accept with the same decoded value digest, or refuse with the same named reason). The runner reads files only (no network, no real time). A mismatch is a finding: red first where it is a reader bug, carried as FIX-CARD: <slug>: <input> <one line>. Do not edit the corpus here; a wrong manifest verdict is reported against the engine card." :brief-file "docs/roadmap-briefs/schema-cards-out-2026-10-19.sexp")
  (:id "sprint-out/schema-shared-12-port-random-differential" :type :task :title "12-port random-input differential (shared port of schema)" :state :todo :evidence nil :sprint-card "schema-shared-12-port-random-differential" :sprint-column "review" :sprint-stream "schema-shared" :sprint-base "sprint/schema-shared" :tier "pro" :needs "" :pushed-head "93d4ba0207700ee960a2eb2bb006e627626ce8a5" :pushed-branch "sprint/schema-shared-12-port-random-differential.w2.g2.e21" :note "Carried: branch sprint/schema-shared-12-port-random-differential.w2.g2.e21 head 93d4ba0207700ee960a2eb2bb006e627626ce8a5 (attempt 2, review). Task: 12-port random-input differential (shared port of schema). Moved out of the sprint on 2026-10-19 (Glenn: \"Please take all work in the current sprint that is not for this rocketnet release and push it out to the appropriate roadmap sexp\"): sprint card schema-shared-12-port-random-differential of stream schema-shared was in review, not landed; the card was dropped from the sprint naming this item, and its pushed head stays on that branch. :brief-file holds the card's whole brief at the move." :task "THE LENS. Schema generates the same algorithm in many languages, so every language's strictest checker, run over the generated output for the schema repository's test-schema corpus (every schema under the corpus directories the Makefile's generate targets read, found with grep -n in the Makefile and make/*.mk; do not invent a second corpus), is a separate lens on bugs (Glenn, 2026-10-18; ideas roadmap group schema-per-language-lenses). THIS CARD: a 12-port differential that sends the same random inputs through every port and compares verdicts (accept/refuse, refusal reason, decoded value), extending the conformance harness over the generated shared output (readers and writers, and the runtime where the port has one). Heavy: nightly." :brief-file "docs/roadmap-briefs/schema-cards-out-2026-10-19.sexp")
  (:id "sprint-out/schema-shared-analyzer-ci-gate-corpus" :type :task :title "Analyzer CI gate over the full corpus (shared port of schema)" :state :todo :evidence nil :sprint-card "schema-shared-analyzer-ci-gate-corpus" :sprint-column "waiting" :sprint-stream "schema-shared" :sprint-base "sprint/schema-shared" :tier "pro" :needs "" :pushed-head "0f8404c537d240339dabd143d778da676ab73a13" :pushed-branch "" :note "Waiting card schema-shared-analyzer-ci-gate-corpus of stream schema-shared, deferred out of the sprint on 2026-10-19 (Glenn: not for the rocketnet v1.0.0 release; moved to the roadmap) with nova-sprint defer; not started in the sprint. It carried an earlier head: schema-shared-analyzer-ci-gate-corpus attempt 1 head 0f8404c537d240339dabd143d778da676ab73a13. :brief-file holds the card's whole brief as defer wrote it." :task "THE LENS. Schema generates the same algorithm in many languages, so every language's strictest checker, run over the generated output for the schema repository's test-schema corpus (every schema under the corpus directories the Makefile's generate targets read, found with grep -n in the Makefile and make/*.mk; do not invent a second corpus), is a separate lens on bugs (Glenn, 2026-10-18; ideas roadmap group schema-per-language-lenses). THIS CARD: every per-port analyzer gate (the sibling cards of the schema-per-language-lenses group) wired as one CI gate over the generated output of the FULL test-schema corpus, with one summary of which analyzers ran, and a check that fails when a port with an analyzer was left out of the corpus run over the generated shared output (readers and writers, and the runtime where the port has one). This card owns the single aggregate target and the nightly workflow job; it calls each port target that exists on the shared base and skips, loudly and by name, those not yet landed. It adds no needs on the sibling cards." :brief-file "docs/roadmap-briefs/schema-cards-out-2026-10-19.sexp")
  (:id "sprint-out/schema-shared-base64-harness-follows-spec-16-2" :type :task :title "The cross-language test/table-base64 harness expects `Q=Q==` to give kind_mismatch; section 16.2 and the ruling say base64_not_canonical, and the tolerant read accepts it" :state :todo :evidence nil :sprint-card "schema-shared-base64-harness-follows-spec-16-2" :sprint-column "waiting" :sprint-stream "schema-go" :sprint-base "sprint/schema-go" :tier "pro" :needs "" :pushed-head "3ad30ed3af15de149b79563230039c645f9b47b7" :pushed-branch "" :note "Waiting card schema-shared-base64-harness-follows-spec-16-2 of stream schema-go, deferred out of the sprint on 2026-10-19 (Glenn: not for the rocketnet v1.0.0 release; moved to the roadmap) with nova-sprint defer; not started in the sprint. It carried an earlier head: schema-shared-base64-harness-follows-spec-16-2 attempt 3 head 3ad30ed3af15de149b79563230039c645f9b47b7. :brief-file holds the card's whole brief as defer wrote it." :task "Source. The coordinator, 2026-10-19. The harness expects an `=` in the middle of a base64 body (`Q=Q==`) to be refused as `kind_mismatch`. docs/SPEC-TABLES.md section 16.2 and the coordinator's ruling on schema-go-json-base64-canonical say it is `base64_not_canonical` (a refusal on the strict read; the tolerant read accepts it and counts it). The harness is also already red at BASE on a different case." :brief-file "docs/roadmap-briefs/schema-cards-out-2026-10-19.sexp")
  (:id "sprint-out/schema-shared-certify-on-fleet" :type :task :title "schema CI: certify.yml (nightly) on the fleet" :state :todo :evidence nil :sprint-card "schema-shared-certify-on-fleet" :sprint-column "waiting" :sprint-stream "schema-shared" :sprint-base "sprint/schema-shared" :tier "pro" :needs "schema-shared-ci-fleet-runners-lint" :pushed-head "" :pushed-branch "" :note "Waiting card schema-shared-certify-on-fleet of stream schema-shared, deferred out of the sprint on 2026-10-19 (Glenn: not for the rocketnet v1.0.0 release; moved to the roadmap) with nova-sprint defer; not started in the sprint. :brief-file holds the card's whole brief as defer wrote it." :task "THE RULE (owner, 2026-10-18): \"all CI should run on our fleet, not github.\" Every job in every workflow runs on the fleet's self-hosted runners, never on a GitHub-hosted label (ubuntu-*, macos-*, windows-*), and never through a fallback expression that resolves to one. A job the fleet cannot run today is never sent to a hosted runner: it is DISABLED explicitly (`if: false` plus a comment `# DISABLED: <reason>; owed: <what turns it back on>`) and its workflow+job pair is a named entry in the lint's exception list with the same reason. Windows jobs are disabled until the Windows fleet machine arrives (no Windows runner is registered; the captain runners are WSL2 Linux and are labelled `slow`). Second rule (owner, 2026-10-18): a workflow never installs tools onto a fleet runner (`npm install -g/--global`, `go install`, `cargo install`, `pip install` outside a job-local venv, `dotnet tool install -g`, `sudo apt-get install`, `brew install`, `luarocks install` without a job-local --tree): the runners are shared machines and a global install overwrites the fleet's pinned toolchain under ~/sdk. The fleet installs and pins every tool through its ansible play; a workflow instead runs a shor [...]" :brief-file "docs/roadmap-briefs/schema-cards-out-2026-10-19.sexp")
  (:id "sprint-out/schema-shared-ci-fleet-runners-lint" :type :task :title "schema CI: the fleet-runner lint, and the small workflows moved to the fleet" :state :todo :evidence nil :sprint-card "schema-shared-ci-fleet-runners-lint" :sprint-column "review" :sprint-stream "schema-shared" :sprint-base "sprint/schema-shared" :tier "pro" :needs "" :pushed-head "fa3035fbcb0dcf4d4defbf91b6c60ff0f1b5fb1f" :pushed-branch "sprint/schema-shared-ci-fleet-runners-lint.w8.g1.e21" :note "Carried: branch sprint/schema-shared-ci-fleet-runners-lint.w8.g1.e21 head fa3035fbcb0dcf4d4defbf91b6c60ff0f1b5fb1f (attempt 10, review). Task: schema CI: the fleet-runner lint, and the small workflows moved to the fleet. Moved out of the sprint on 2026-10-19 (Glenn: \"Please take all work in the current sprint that is not for this rocketnet release and push it out to the appropriate roadmap sexp\"): sprint card schema-shared-ci-fleet-runners-lint of stream schema-shared was in review, not landed; the card was dropped from the sprint naming this item, and its pushed head stays on that branch. :brief-file holds the card's whole brief at the move." :task "THE RULE (owner, 2026-10-18): \"all CI should run on our fleet, not github.\" Every job in every workflow runs on the fleet's self-hosted runners, never on a GitHub-hosted label (ubuntu-*, macos-*, windows-*), and never through a fallback expression that resolves to one. A job the fleet cannot run today is never sent to a hosted runner: it is DISABLED explicitly (`if: false` plus a comment `# DISABLED: <reason>; owed: <what turns it back on>`) and its workflow+job pair is a named entry in the lint's exception list with the same reason. Windows jobs are disabled until the Windows fleet machine arrives (no Windows runner is registered; the captain runners are WSL2 Linux and are labelled `slow`). Second rule (owner, 2026-10-18): a workflow never installs tools onto a fleet runner (`npm install -g/--global`, `go install`, `cargo install`, `pip install` outside a job-local venv, `dotnet tool install -g`, `sudo apt-get install`, `brew install`, `luarocks install` without a job-local --tree): the runners are shared machines and a global install overwrites the fleet's pinned toolchain under ~/sdk. The fleet installs and pins every tool through its ansible play; a workflow instead runs a shor [...]" :brief-file "docs/roadmap-briefs/schema-cards-out-2026-10-19.sexp")
  (:id "sprint-out/schema-shared-ci-full-on-fleet" :type :task :title "schema CI: ci-full.yml on the fleet" :state :todo :evidence nil :sprint-card "schema-shared-ci-full-on-fleet" :sprint-column "waiting" :sprint-stream "schema-shared" :sprint-base "sprint/schema-shared" :tier "pro" :needs "schema-shared-ci-fleet-runners-lint" :pushed-head "" :pushed-branch "" :note "Waiting card schema-shared-ci-full-on-fleet of stream schema-shared, deferred out of the sprint on 2026-10-19 (Glenn: not for the rocketnet v1.0.0 release; moved to the roadmap) with nova-sprint defer; not started in the sprint. :brief-file holds the card's whole brief as defer wrote it." :task "THE RULE (owner, 2026-10-18): \"all CI should run on our fleet, not github.\" Every job in every workflow runs on the fleet's self-hosted runners, never on a GitHub-hosted label (ubuntu-*, macos-*, windows-*), and never through a fallback expression that resolves to one. A job the fleet cannot run today is never sent to a hosted runner: it is DISABLED explicitly (`if: false` plus a comment `# DISABLED: <reason>; owed: <what turns it back on>`) and its workflow+job pair is a named entry in the lint's exception list with the same reason. Windows jobs are disabled until the Windows fleet machine arrives (no Windows runner is registered; the captain runners are WSL2 Linux and are labelled `slow`). Second rule (owner, 2026-10-18): a workflow never installs tools onto a fleet runner (`npm install -g/--global`, `go install`, `cargo install`, `pip install` outside a job-local venv, `dotnet tool install -g`, `sudo apt-get install`, `brew install`, `luarocks install` without a job-local --tree): the runners are shared machines and a global install overwrites the fleet's pinned toolchain under ~/sdk. The fleet installs and pins every tool through its ansible play; a workflow instead runs a shor [...]" :brief-file "docs/roadmap-briefs/schema-cards-out-2026-10-19.sexp")
  (:id "sprint-out/schema-shared-differential-fuzz" :type :task :title "nightly fuzzing (shared port of schema)" :state :todo :evidence nil :sprint-card "schema-shared-differential-fuzz" :sprint-column "review" :sprint-stream "schema-shared" :sprint-base "sprint/schema-shared" :tier "pro" :needs "" :pushed-head "54c826b66ff9e5737b82a63a33564b1be21f4f33" :pushed-branch "sprint/schema-shared-differential-fuzz.w6.g2.e21" :note "Carried: branch sprint/schema-shared-differential-fuzz.w6.g2.e21 head 54c826b66ff9e5737b82a63a33564b1be21f4f33 (attempt 8, review). Task: nightly fuzzing (shared port of schema). Moved out of the sprint on 2026-10-19 (Glenn: \"Please take all work in the current sprint that is not for this rocketnet release and push it out to the appropriate roadmap sexp\"): sprint card schema-shared-differential-fuzz of stream schema-shared was in review, not landed; the card was dropped from the sprint naming this item, and its pushed head stays on that branch. :brief-file holds the card's whole brief at the move." :task "NIGHTLY FUZZING (Glenn, 2026-10-18). Fuzz the shared port's generated readers with its native coverage-guided fuzzer: a mutation fuzzer feeding every port. Targets: load, strict read and text/JSON parse for every table in a fuzz corpus schema set (pick the set from the schema repository's test-schema corpus (every schema under the corpus directories the Makefile's generate targets read, found with grep -n in the Makefile and make/*.mk; do not invent a second corpus) so that every table shape is covered, and list it in a file the harness reads). Seed the fuzzer from the Go fuzz corpus (internal/fuzz/testdata and the go test -fuzz seeds) and the conformance vectors. Each mutated input goes through every port, and the verdicts must agree: accept or refuse, the refusal reason, and the decoded value. A disagreement is a finding saved as a regression input in the shared conformance vectors. Reuse the harness of the 12-port random-input differential card (schema-shared-12-port-random-differential) if it has landed; otherwise build the smallest driver and say so." :brief-file "docs/roadmap-briefs/schema-cards-out-2026-10-19.sexp")
  (:id "sprint-out/schema-shared-resource-bounds-every-port" :type :task :title "Resource bounds: the documented factor, the depth cap and the engine reference (shared port of schema)" :state :todo :evidence nil :sprint-card "schema-shared-resource-bounds-every-port" :sprint-column "waiting" :sprint-stream "schema-shared" :sprint-base "sprint/schema-shared" :tier "pro" :needs "" :pushed-head "216dc846ccf497be2d225444f347bdefcb2fe978" :pushed-branch "" :note "Waiting card schema-shared-resource-bounds-every-port of stream schema-shared, deferred out of the sprint on 2026-10-19 (Glenn: not for the rocketnet v1.0.0 release; moved to the roadmap) with nova-sprint defer; not started in the sprint. It carried an earlier head: schema-shared-resource-bounds-every-port attempt 2 head 216dc846ccf497be2d225444f347bdefcb2fe978. :brief-file holds the card's whole brief as defer wrote it." :task "Glenn, 2026-10-18: denial-of-service hardening for every port. THIS CARD DEFINES the bounds all ports are held to, and holds the Go engine and Go generated readers to them first. Decide and document in docs/SPEC-TABLES.md (normative, with row ids when schema-spec-pin-design-row-ids has landed; else plain MUST sentences): the allocation factor (bytes allocated by a read are at most input size times F, state F and why), the nesting depth cap and the refusal name for exceeding it, and the shape of a hostile resource test (huge counts, deep nesting, recursion, giant strings, many unknown fields). Add the refusal name to the engine and to the generator contract. Implement and test the bounds in the Go engine and the Go generated readers with an allocation counter (testing.AllocsPerRun or runtime.MemStats, with no real time). Then the 12 per-port cards (schema-<port>-resource-bounds) apply it in each language." :brief-file "docs/roadmap-briefs/schema-cards-out-2026-10-19.sexp")
  (:id "sprint-out/schema-spec-pin-s2" :type :task :title "Pin the normative sentences of section 2 (Declaration, 2.1 to 2.11) (shared port of schema)" :state :todo :evidence nil :sprint-card "schema-spec-pin-s2" :sprint-column "ready" :sprint-stream "schema-shared" :sprint-base "sprint/schema-shared" :tier "pro" :needs "" :pushed-head "07e419a12f0a0e2d8bff38013255cc4369cfbe0f" :pushed-branch "sprint/schema-spec-pin-s2.w6.g1.e21" :note "Carried: branch sprint/schema-spec-pin-s2.w6.g1.e21 head 07e419a12f0a0e2d8bff38013255cc4369cfbe0f (attempt 6, ready). Task: Pin the normative sentences of section 2 (Declaration, 2.1 to 2.11) (shared port of schema). Moved out of the sprint on 2026-10-19 (Glenn: \"Please take all work in the current sprint that is not for this rocketnet release and push it out to the appropriate roadmap sexp\"): sprint card schema-spec-pin-s2 of stream schema-shared was in ready, not landed; the card was dropped from the sprint naming this item, and its pushed head stays on that branch. :brief-file holds the card's whole brief at the move." :task "Apply the design of schema-spec-pin-design-row-ids (read it first; the row-id syntax, the pin format and the drift guard are its) to section 2 (Declaration, 2.1 to 2.11) of docs/SPEC-TABLES.md: give every MUST, MUST NOT and refusal sentence a row id, and pin each to a test in every port that carries the feature. A sentence with no test in some port gets a NEW test there, written red first at BASE where the behaviour is wrong; a sentence the code does not satisfy is a finding: carry it in the report as FIX-CARD: <slug>: <row id> <one line>. The drift guard must be green for this section's rows. Do not touch other sections." :brief-file "docs/roadmap-briefs/schema-cards-out-2026-10-19.sexp")
